msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_9@NAME"
msgstr "Undead Lichbringers"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_ARACHNA@BIO"
msgstr "A spinner of exquisite crafting, she sings a luring melody from the hidden place, feeling the vibrations in the strings of her many tangled web. The weaver Arachna spins intrigue, ensnaring lost souls that wander into darkness to hide their shame. Her dark servants move about the world, while she lurks deep in the nest of shadows.[br/][br/]Arachna discovered that some Goblins were so distasteful that her beloved spiders refused to consume them. With that, her Reclusive Spiderlings were born. These symbiotic fiends love lurking unnoticed in the recesses of the world. They breed their arachnids, which have now grown to such enormous proportions that they ride them into combat."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_CINREN@BIO"
msgstr "An attractive elf who nevertheless evokes an aura of haughty superiority, Cinren wears a perpetual sneer of lecherous intent. It is said that he has devoted much of his existence to the magical honing of carnal delights, often careening down dark and morally ambiguous pathways in order to reach undiscovered realms of pleasure.[br/][br/]The group of elves known as the Ashborn Hedonists follow Cinren Toliath and revere his godlike pursuit of pleasure. Powerful practitioners of magic in their own right, they seek to bring all under the sway of their master in order to provide more fodder towards his lecherous machinations."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_DISCARDEDAI@BIO"
msgstr "Once, Otto was Nimue's eighth favorite, and for a short while everything was good. Being abandoned by his Goddess initiated his ascension to Godirhood, although he fears what these powers may do to him. Now he leads the people who call themselves Recreants, wearing the shame of Nimue's abandonment as a banner. Whether Godirhood is a blessing or a curse to the created Otto… only time will tell.[br/][br/]The Drowned Recreants were once named Nimue's Chosen Children and a friend to beast and man alike. They were loved by their Goddess, and they loved her in return. She, however, eventually grew disappointed with their flaws and discarded them, drowning many in her wrath. Now, those who remain call themselves the Drowned Recreants and are trying to start a civilization of their own, though many still fear the wrath of their former Goddess."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_ELEANOR@BIO"
msgstr "Once a proud and powerful Elven Empress beside her husband Inioch, Eleanor perished giving birth to her son, Prince Meandor. Her soul wandered to {GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, where a tomb was created to honor her, protecting her from the ills the origin world of the Elves had to endure."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_INIOCH@BIO"
msgstr "Once the uncontested sovereign of the Valley of Wonders, Inioch refused to yield to the divine contracts that anointed his divine right to rule. Turning against all that was holy, he plumbed the depths of death. Now, he is little but a fragmented soul, unable to reach the Well of Creation and what lies beyond."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_KHIR@BIO"
msgstr "The name Khir Uranon has often been spoken in dreaded whisper. Those that know his name know him to be a demonic manipulator, whose mastery of the forge is fueled by a callous disregard for the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept]souls[/hyperlink] he infuses his creations with.[br/][br/]The Blackfurred Forgelings are known for their prodigious strength and merciless cruelty, both aspects forged in the fires of their masters' ancient crucibles. Here, they help him utilize the souls of those that fall before them to power demonic artifacts."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_LITHYL@BIO"
msgstr "Rumors surround the origins of enigmatic Lithyl Nightweaver, the half-masked wizard who seemed to appear from the Astral Void itself. Shortly after her arrival on Magehaven she joined the Shad'rai on their quest for power over others. Charming and conniving, she seems to be one of many mad Godir, haunted by her Torment of Shadows. But Lithyl specifically stands out for her talent of appearing and disappearing at opportune times.[br/][br/]Not all who wander the Astral Sea are Godir. Many mortals find themselves lost in its depths, forgotten, with no divine power to save them. One Godir has taken it upon herself to save these lost souls. Lithyl Nightweaver reaches out an eldritch hand to pull the Forgotten Ones from the void, no matter how haunted and scarred it left them. Whatever her ulterior motives may be, Lithyl has won her people's undying devotion."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_LOYALISTAI@BIO"
msgstr "Decimus was hand-picked by Nimue as a Ruler of her then latest created race, and proudly named Nimue's tenth favorite. He wore this honor with pride and responsibility, until his creator Goddess grew disappointed with him and his people for reasons unknown to any but herself. It was this guilt that led him to pursue a life of righteousness for him and his people, and it was this weight of responsibility that started him on his path to ascension. [br/][br/]The Atoning Toadmen were created by Nimue and once rose above many others, but must now answer for their sins. What sins and how, they are not sure, but they must atone nonetheless, and lead others on the same path of righteousness before their former Goddess, Nimue, can love them again. "

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_MEANDOR@BIO"
msgstr "A harbinger of intrigue, Meandor is the first Prince of the ancient tradition of Dark Elves. He plots against allies and enemies alike. He once experienced death and found it unsatisfying. He now respects his sister Julia, but won't hesitate to stab a dagger through her plans. His followers see him as a symbol of vengeance, but he prefers to shirk ideologies. He revels in remaining a wild card in the realm of diplomatic games. Yet, he, too, is haunted by his own demons.[br/][br/]Dark Elves lurk in the deep shadows, plotting vengeance upon humanity and the fair races that tolerate them. They will never forget how men stole their lands. Dark Elves enslave weaker races and train them in cruelty, using them to achieve their nefarious purposes. They are masters of stealth, known to favor a well placed blade in the back over a fair fight. "

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_MEANDOR_DLC4@BIO"
msgstr "Since his return to {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, after the events on {GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, Meandor has demonstrated much responsibility and leadership in the attempts of the {GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to bring structure and order to the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. None of this he would openly admit however, as he still prefers to be regarded as a lord of shadow and death.[br/][br/]The Swarming Hammers emerged in a frenzy when the influence of the Chaos Endailon had stirred up war on many worlds. When they became denounced as pests that the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} should eradicate, Meandor stepped in to take them under his care. Through him they learned to channel their ceaseless energy into the creation of monumental structures and rune-enchanted artisanry. Though Meandor seeks to mentor them into independence, ruled by a champion of their own, the Swarming Hammers still revere him as their swarm king, eager to pave any way he desires to walk."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_NIMUE@BIO"
msgstr "Her mind is a torrent of unpredictable chaos. She wills it and her children rise from the surge, breathing her very lifeblood. Like the tide beating against the changing coastline, so too is Nimue among the Godir. Her power is undeniable, yet her moods swirl like waves in a tide pool. Her children all accept that, inevitably, all will find themselves drowned in a watery grave.[br/][br/]Obsequious and ever condescending, Nimue's Chosen Children know that their time as her favored creations is limited, and if they're not careful, they will all end up drowned in the depths. Fortunately, these clever amphibians have an affinity for water, and know ways of quietly slipping beneath the surface when her storms start churning up the muck."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_SARIDAS@BIO"
msgstr "Saridas was once a Dark Elven advisor to Prince Meandor. Later, he married Queen Julia, thus becoming king of the High Elves on Athla. He suffered dearly from the loss of his only son, Thannis, and almost threw his empire into an all-out war. His quest for vengeance only stopped due to his own daughter, Sundren. Of course, the life of a king is never safe... and in the years following the Third Age, Saridas found his demise after the seals of Athla were broken. His soul traveled to {GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept.Hyperlink} where he was reunited with his son. Now, he is forced to stay on this realm until a Godir breaks the curse that affects it."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_SHIRA@BIO"
msgstr "Shira was born the heir of her people. During her coronation, the Shad'rai invaded her realm, killed her family and cast her into the Astral Void. Shira would have been Lost if not for the aid of Meandor, who guided her to Magehaven, where she joined the Covenant and learned to channel her grief into primal prowess. After a heroic return and a fierce battle against the usurping Shad'rai Godir, she retook her homeland.[br/][br/]Arctic Felines are a proud people who adjusted to the icy tundra of Cantarra, their homeworld. After the return of their long-lost Queen, they followed her through the depths of the Astral Sea and back to avenge their fallen royal family and thwart the plans of the Shad'rai."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_SUNDREN@BIO"
msgstr "Curious and clever, Sundren was the second-born child, daughter of Queen Julia and her royal consort. She founded the Torchbearers as one of the few leaders ever to unite High Elves with their Dark-Elf kindred... But after the assassination of her brother, and later the death of her father, Sundren finds her noble heart growing dark with a lust for vengeance.[br/][br/]Mended Torchbearers are the kindred and followers of Sundred and her dream of a life filled with a deeply heroic meaning. Many kindred were once jaded by age and propriety, while others thirsted for bloody revenge. Sundren gave them all a much more thrilling reason to live. "

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_THANNIS@BIO"
msgstr "Many mourn the loss of the High Elven prodigy, Thannis, the first High Elf born on Athla after the mending of the Dark and Wood Elves. His unjustified death caused empires to clash and threw Athla into an all-out war, only brought to an end by the heroic actions of his rebellious sister, Sundren. His soul wandered to {GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the origin world of all Elves, where he remains, not necessarily voluntarily."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@RACE_YAKA@BIO"
msgstr "Stare into the flames long enough and a single name will come to your lips. A god of fire. Only a god of fire can live within the raging inferno, able to master its unpredictable flow of destruction. He is quick to punish those that do not give him rightful reverence, for only creatures that can withstand waves of unrelenting heat are worthy to serve the great Godir, Yaka.[br/][br/]Remembering a time when felines were worshiped as god-kin, the Firebrand Predators serve Yaka with a zeal that he has not seen for generations. Yaka dotes upon his Tigran followers, for he remembers how his past servants abandoned him. Together they seek to build an unquenchable inferno."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@TURIEL@BIO"
msgstr "A mighty Orc whose honor-bound convictions match his prodigious strength, Turiel was the first Wizard King to ascend to Godirhood. He appears as a mighty and masked Orc, a bastion of stoic ferocity clad in indomitable armor and wielding brutal weaponry. Ever oath-bound to the Archon in guarding Grexolis, he holds honor and duty in highest esteem.[br/][br/]Turiel leads the mighty Onmar, fierce Ascended Orcs who aid him in a duty shared and who have, in return, been blessed by the Archon. Their minds are guarded against the insidious whispers of the banished souls they hold eternal vigil over. "

msgid "CAMPAIGN@LORDS@YDGAARD@BIO"
msgstr "Like the Void Stone that replaced his heart through a macabre covenant for power, Ydgaard's desires run to the cold and shiny. A grizzled and mighty Dwarf whose greed is as impressive as his beard, he covets wealth and resources above all. The great jewel that adorns his left eye socket in place of an eyeball (also part of the aforementioned pact) is a stark reflection of how he sees the world. [br/][br/]Ydgaard rules over a race of mole-like beings known as the Grave Underlings. It is surmised that their form was chosen due in part to their poor eyesight, that they may never covet their master's wealth. Likewise, their natural predilection to excavation of the planet's riches allow them to ever increase the size of Ydgaard's own hoard."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "It was the time when the raw forces of magic returned to Athla. The seal that had protected the world was shattered, the cosmic currents thereby unleashed shaped the land, changing what was whilst returning what once may have been. In the wake of this new genesis, the great empires of the Third Age fell into decline, bringing on an era of re-exploration and expansion."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Alas, the time for peaceful discovery was brief, for the ancient wizards of the Second Age broke free from their eldritch prisons in the depths of the Astral Sea. Their strength regained, they set out to rule over the surviving peoples as god-kings, or Godir."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@BRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "There was little divine about them. Yaka, Nimue, Karissa—a pantheon of pretender gods. They were scarred, corrupted, haunted by millennia of torment—and ready to unleash their newfound powers against whoever dared stand in their way."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@BRIEFING_04@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Yet the Wizard Kings were not unchallenged. Mortal champions rose to the defense of their people, rebuilding their realms and learning to channel the currents of magic."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@BRIEFING_05@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is the story of one such champion. While traveling through the Valley of Wonders in search of a new home, tragedy befell <<o:HeroFirstName>> tribe, its elder slain by a magical being. After inheriting both the elder’s throne and his powerful Tome of Magic, the young champion had to rise up and protect <<o:HeroFirstName>> people from the dangers that awaited them."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "By repelling the invasion of Yaka, the spark of divinity was ignited, and a new Godir ascended to the cosmic Pantheon. Beyond the veil of mortality, the Pantheon represented an entirely different world. For while the Godir could walk the realms as gods, they had to abide by rules when dealing with their own kin within the Astral Sea."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@DEBRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In Magehaven, a world near the center of the Astral Sea, the Godir of the Pantheon had established their forum of counsel. It was a place warded by an ancient spell. Stripped of their abilities to harm one another, even the fiercest enemies could meet up in Magehaven. Here the Godir constructed their World Gates, through which they embarked on their journeys of exploration and expansion that defined the Fourth Age of Wonders."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "As a mortal champion, build up a new home for your wandering tribe in the mythical Valley of Wonders. Prepare yourself for the clash with the returning Wizard Kings of old and rise in power to claim a greater destiny."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@NAME"
msgstr "Valley of Wonders"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_00@SUB_HEADER"
msgstr "As an {GLOBAL.AscendedChampLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, build up a new home for your wandering tribe in the mythical {GLOBAL.ValleyofWondersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Prepare yourself for the clash with the returning <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> of old and rise in power to claim a greater destiny."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Astral Sea connects all and everything. To most, it is merely a way to travel between worlds, yet some call the Astral Sea itself their home. Of the many beings who reside within, the curious Maer are the most gentle. They swim through the magical currents with ease and use their voices to guide lost souls to safety. This is the story of one such Maer called Elya, whose curiosity led her to misery."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "The Maer"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This particular young Maer was intrigued by the worlds that connect to the Astral Sea. She was specifically attracted to a realm called the Enchanted Archipelago, for its tides resembled her natural habitat, yet felt so different. But it did not take long before Elya's visit turned into a nightmare, when she was captured by a capricious Godir called Nimue who sought to study her for her beauty and power."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_02@TITLE"
msgstr "Capture"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The self-proclaimed \"Goddess\" Nimue used Elya in her efforts to create her ultimate race of followers… but her results never lived up to her ever-shifting demands. Elya was forced to watch Nimue drown her own creations over and over again, only to begin anew once more. The horrified Elya, shackled and sequestered, could only sing a desperate song, carried by the currents over the Astral Sea."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_03@TITLE"
msgstr "A Desperate Song"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_04@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Elya's song reached Magehaven, where the Covenant, a virtuous alliance of Godir, heard her plea. The Covenant sought to uphold the ancient agreements of peace and stability, and were thus concerned by the song about Nimue. Had the Siren Goddess gone mad with power, or was another force at play? One zealous Godir of the Covenant volunteered to investigate the Enchanted Archipelago and liberate it from Nimue's drowning embrace."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@BRIEFING_04@TITLE"
msgstr "The Savior"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Thus was the Siren Goddess defeated and the Enchanted Archipelago freed from her obsessive grasp. And Elya, the curious Maer who euphorically experienced freedom once more… I am her. It was I who witnessed both the terror and grace of the Godir. It is for this reason that I sing the stories of this Age of Godir and of the good and the evil that reside within the ever-flowing Astral Sea."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "The Goddess, Defeated"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Yet my freedom begets responsibility. I could no longer ignore the murder and destruction of the powerless and innocent. My time as prisoner taught me about the plans of Nimue and her allies, the Godir alliance who call themselves the Shad'rai. This is why I had to inform the Covenant about the scheming Shad'rai and their ambitions—which were far greater than what the Covenant imagined."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_02@TITLE"
msgstr "Dark Plans"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Become an ambassador of the Covenant and venture to the Enchanted Archipelago, where a once Banished Wizard is abusing the currents of Creation. Investigate the goals of the Shad'rai alliance and free the realm from the Siren Goddess."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@NAME"
msgstr "Enchanted Archipelago"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_01@SUB_HEADER"
msgstr "Become an ambassador of the {GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and venture to the Enchanted Archipelago on {GLOBAL.TidolonLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, where a once banished {GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is abusing the currents of Creation. Investigate the goals of the {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} alliance and free the realm from the Siren Goddess."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Ages ago, when the Astral Sea was still young, the Archons created a magical artifact. Forged in the fires of an Elder Dragon, the Gildercoil served as an arcane compass, guiding the Archons through the currents between realms. According to legend, it still contains the echoes of their arcane journeys, and can lead those who hold it to forgotten places of sealed knowledge and magic."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "Visions of Sand"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "With its mysterious promise of power, the Gildercoil fanned the greed of many rulers, until a daring Godir betrayed the Archons and stole the Gildercoil from their Celestial Reliquary. Ever since then, all traces of the compass have been lost, as have those of the cunning thief who disappeared into the mists of time."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_02@TITLE"
msgstr "The False God"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Or so it seemed for many a lifetime... Lithyl Nightweaver was the first of the Shad'rai to find clues of the Gildercoil's whereabouts—myths, leading to runic omens, leading to riddles. The Shad'rai were persistent in their search, for too well did the Archon artifact fit into their unfolding plans. And they were rewarded."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_03@NAME"
msgstr "Crimson Caldera"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@BRIEFING_04@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In the infernal world of Obbadoth, there exists a realm known as the Crimson Caldera, where war is eternal. Here the Gildercoil lay hidden. Yet the Shad'rai sought no open conflict with Obbadoth's demonic princes. As they weighed their options, an ambitious Godir from their ranks volunteered to venture there alone, well aware of the prestige and power that could be gained within their order."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Thus, by the hands of the Shad'rai, the wicked scheme of Frikka Dynosis had been revealed, and the Gildercoil was recovered. The Crimson Caldera had met its champion and even the princes of Obbadoth dared not interfere."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "Chaos Mission Debriefing 01"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "As an agent of the Shad'rai, venture to a demonic realm of never-ending war to search for an ancient Archon artifact of power. Become the victor in an arena of mad violence and end the curse that brought doom upon so many aspiring kings and Godir."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@MAP@NAME"
msgstr "Crimson Caldera"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_02@SUB_HEADER"
msgstr "As an agent of the {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, venture to a demonic realm of never-ending war to search for an ancient [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink] artifact of power. Become the victor in an arena of mad violence and end the curse of {GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, which brought doom upon so many aspiring kings and {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_03@TITLE"
msgstr "The Shad'rai Plot: Smelter Mountains (Ertra Anov)"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "After seizing the Gildercoil, the Shad'rai suddenly disappeared. This concerned most Godir, the members of the Covenant in particular, who were actively opposed to the Shad'rai and their schemes. However, none knew how to follow the Shad'rai, or what their destination was. The Covenant convened in Magehaven to debate."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "Concern amongst the Covenant"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Athlan ruler Sundren proposed to seek out Prince Meandor, her uncle. Meandor was a powerful Wizard of Death and the heir of the fallen House Inioch. He was the first Athlan to discover Magehaven and had guided many banished wizards there, including the Shad'rai, saving them from eternal torment in the darkness that lay between the realms. If anyone could track down the Shad'rai wizards, it was Meandor."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_02@TITLE"
msgstr "Prince of Shadows"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "However, for reasons unknown or unfortunate, Meandor had elected to exile himself to Auldweald, the ancient home world of the Elves, where he established a realm for himself. Since then, concerning reports had reached Magehaven. The shadow of death had washed over the vibrant forests, its cities haunted by lingering souls and roaming spirits who were unable to finish their journeys to the Well of Creation."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_03@TITLE"
msgstr "Eternal Court"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_04@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Many Elves had since fled the realm, reporting that Meandor was responsible for its fall. He had vowed to restore his beloved lost Elven Court to its old glory. Dark magic followed him and his apparitions as he turned the realm itself against anyone who dared enter his waking dream of the past. The Covenant saw no choice but to send a fearless Godir to reclaim this Eternal Court from the renegade Wizard of Shadows."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@BRIEFING_04@TITLE"
msgstr "A Ghostly Curse"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A fearless Godir of the Covenant broke Meandor's curse and freed the souls trapped within the Eternal Court. After his recovery in Magehaven, Meandor explained he had uncovered the plans of the Shad'rai and their search for the Gildercoil. The Covenant's concerns about the Shad'rai were justified, for the Gildercoil was not just a compass… It was a powerful Archon artifact, capable of leading those wielding it to powers even legends dared not mention."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@DEBRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Shad'rai sought to release the power locked away by the Archons. They had invited Meandor to join their cause, but after his refusal, the dark cabal had ensnared him in the nightmares of his past. Meandor was furious that he had allowed himself to be manipulated. He thus decided to aid the Covenant and used his strong connection to the Astral Sea to locate the Shad'rai. But before the other Godir could follow, he issued a warning."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@DEBRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "After spending an age clinging to the past, Meandor concluded that the flow of the Astral Sea could not be compelled or defied. He sensed anticipation within the currents: forces from the dawn of time would imminently resurface. The Shad'rai may have been unscrupulous in their search for this power but, deep down, all Godir lust for it. Meandor bitterly declared that a Godir has but one choice: Follow the pulls of the tide... or seek oblivion, as he did."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Join the Covenant once more to investigate the haunted forests of the Auldweald, origin world of the Elves. Confront the mad Wizard who has cast the realm into the shadows of undeath and free the trapped spirits within."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@NAME"
msgstr "The Eternal Court"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_CONQUER_ARACHNA@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Spellweaver Defeated"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_DEFEAT_INIOCH@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Fallen Emperor Defeated"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_DEFEAT_SARIDAS"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Spirit of Saridas Defeated"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_FIND_ARACHNA@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Spellweaver Found"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_FIND_INIOCH@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Fallen Emperor Found"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_FIND_SARIDAS"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Entity Found"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_FREE_ELEANOR@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Tomb Explored"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@QUEST_FREE_ELEANOR_AFFINITY@OBJECTIVE"
msgstr "{INT_0}/{INT_1} Lost Mother Freed"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@SUB_HEADER"
msgstr "Join the {GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} once more to investigate the haunted forests of {GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, origin world of the elves. Confront the mad {GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who has cast the realm into the shadows of undeath, and free the trapped {GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} within."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_05@TOMB_ELEANOR@NAME"
msgstr "Tomb of the Lost Mother"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "\"Glory to all Godir and glory to the Shad'rai!\" The rousing hymn of the Shad'rai was heard far and wide as they gathered to use the Gildercoil and embark from Magehaven to challenge the Archons themselves. For too long had archaic Archon dogmas controlled the cosmos and determined what should exist and what shouldn't. It was time to ring in a new age and break the chains that fettered the true potential of the Pantheon."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@BRIEFING_01@TITLE"
msgstr "Grexolis"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Grexolis was the long-sought-after target of the Shad'rai. It was a world whose mere existence had been concealed by the Archons in great effort, as it contained the forbidden magic of ancient times. The Gildercoil not only guided the Shad'rai to Grexolis—it was the very key to opening the World Vault itself. Coming to Grexolis meant to seek celestial judgment. But the Shad'rai were prepared."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The battle had been fierce, but at last the Shad'rai overwhelmed the Covenant and Turiel, guardian of Grexolis. Their victory, however, became tainted with confusion when Lithyl Nightweaver revealed her true identity. And then, she broke the World Vault. Grexolis burst open in a swirl of raw magic, an arcane tide surging through the Astral Sea. In the blink of an eye, entire worlds came to be anew while a myriad of forgotten thoughts invaded the minds of the present Godir."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@DEBRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "As the turmoil slowly subsided, the Shad'rai convened on the empty shell of Grexolis to reflect on their achievement. They had caught a glimpse of something great, a veil lifted on ancient times and its primal gods. Forgotten were all worries about the Archons and their distant war with the Shadow. For the realms of the altered cosmos glimmered like beacons of magic mystery—as if they were beckoning Magehaven's Godir to rise in this Fourth Age of Wonders."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "As the spearhead of a Shad'rai alliance, invade the fractured world Grexolis hidden in the mists of the Astral Sea. Face the custodian, whom the Archons left on this world to guard the ancient magic which lies buried here."

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@NAME"
msgstr "Grexolis"

msgid "CAMPAIGN@MISSION_06@SUB_HEADER"
msgstr "As the spearhead of a {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} alliance, invade the fractured world {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink} hidden in the mists of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Face the custodian, which the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} left on this world to guard the ancient magic which lies buried here."

