msgstr "Defenseless Attackers"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_ARMOR_ENEMIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "All defending units have {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SUNDERED_DEFENSE.Hyperlink} until the end of battle."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_ARMOR_ENEMIES@NAME"
msgstr "Defenseless Defenders"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_RESISTANCE_ARMY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "All attacking units have {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SUNDERED_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink} until the end of battle."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_RESISTANCE_ARMY@NAME"
msgstr "Vulnerable Attackers"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_RESISTANCE_ENEMIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "All defending units have {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SUNDERED_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink} until the end of battle."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_RESISTANCE_ENEMIES@NAME"
msgstr "Vulnerable Defenders"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_STATUS_RESISTANCE_ARMY@NAME"
msgstr "Sundered Status Resistance Attackers"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@SUNDERED_STATUS_RESISTANCE_ENEMIES@NAME"
msgstr "Sundered Status Resistance Defenders"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@THE_ONE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Every {GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}, the attacker's units lose {MoraleValue} morale."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@THE_ONE@NAME"
msgstr "The Wailing"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@UNDEADQUEEN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Killing the Undead Queen will immediately kill all of her [abilityred]Undead Servants[/abilityred]."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@UNDEADQUEEN@NAME"
msgstr "Undead Queen"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WAVE_OF_TRANQUILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Every {turn} <<m:{GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}>>, all Status Effects on all units are dispelled."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WAVE_OF_TRANQUILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Wave of Tranquility"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WEAKENED_ARMY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "All attacking units become {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.WEAKENED.Hyperlink} until the end of battle."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WEAKENED_ARMY@NAME"
msgstr "Weakened Attackers"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WEAKENED_ENEMIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "All defending units become {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.WEAKENED.Hyperlink} until the end of battle."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WEAKENED_ENEMIES@NAME"
msgstr "Weakened Defenders"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WINTERS_SORROW@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Enemy units suffer {amount} stack(s) of {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DEMORALIZED.Hyperlink} whenever they kill another unit."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WINTERS_SORROW@NAME"
msgstr "Winter Sorrow"

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WINTERS_SORROW@SECTOR_DISPLAY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.COMBATPROPERTY_FEY_WINTER.Hyperlink} is active in this province."

msgid "COMBATPROPERTIES_TACTICAL@WINTERS_SORROW@SECTOR_DISPLAY@NAME"
msgstr "Domain of Winter"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACCURACY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} has a ranged ability selected. Ranged abilities have an {GLOBAL.AccuracyConcept} rating, which is the chance of the ability hitting the intended target."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACCURACY@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "If an ability misses, it will either strike another target or do nothing at all. Some abilities can also graze, meaning that the ability affected the target but with reduced strength."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACCURACY@TITLE"
msgstr "Accuracy"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "You have selected a {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}. It has 3 <<m:{GLOBAL.ActionPointConcept}>> to spend on moving and using abilities."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "Different abilities have different [actionpoint/] action point costs, and some trigger once per action point available. Using an ability will almost always end a unit's turn![br/][br/]As you plan movement, you can see the number of [fullaction/] action points you will have available at your destination."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ACTION_POINTS@TITLE"
msgstr "Action Points"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@AI_TAKEOVER_NPC@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "You have temporarily taken command of an Independent army.[br/][br/]While in control of a {GLOBAL.IndependentCityConcept.Hyperlink} or <<m:GLOBAL.MarauderConcept.Hyperlink>>, you are able to issue orders to their <<m:GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink>>. The ability to cast <<m:GLOBAL.CombatSpellConcept.Hyperlink>> is disabled during the Independent turn."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@AI_TAKEOVER_NPC@TITLE"
msgstr "Combat Takeover: Independents"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@AI_TAKEOVER_PLAYER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "You have temporarily taken command of an army belonging to an AI {GLOBAL.LeaderConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]When taking over for an AI Ruler, you can command their <<m:GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink>> and make use of their <<m:GLOBAL.CombatSpellConcept.Hyperlink>> during combat."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@AI_TAKEOVER_PLAYER@TITLE"
msgstr "Combat Takeover: AI Ruler"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@BATTLE_MAGE_UNITS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Battle Mage {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, which excels at dealing magical damage and applying status effects. It is vulnerable to {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} attacks and should be kept in the back line."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@BATTLE_MAGE_UNITS@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitBattleMage/]Battle Mage Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@CASUALTIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} has suffered <<m:{GLOBAL.CasualtyConcept}>>. Casualties occur when a unit takes damage, which also causes the unit to deal less damage with its attacks."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@CASUALTIES@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "Units that are represented by a single figure, such as <<m:{GLOBAL.HeroConcept}>> and giants, are immune to casualties."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@CASUALTIES@TITLE"
msgstr "Casualties"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@COMBAT_STARTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Welcome to the field of battle! Here you must kill or rout your foes in order to claim victory."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@COMBAT_STARTS@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "The defending {GLOBAL.ArmyConcept} always takes the first turn, followed by the attacking army."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@COMBAT_STARTS@TITLE"
msgstr "Battle Commences"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@FLANKING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Your {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} just attacked an enemy from behind. This is called {GLOBAL.FlankingConcept}, and gives a damage bonus."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@FLANKING@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "Remember that units in {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink} cannot be flanked!"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@FLANKING@TITLE"
msgstr "Flanking Attacks"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LEADER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "You have selected your {GLOBAL.LeaderConcept}. Your Ruler is a powerful combatant who can wield magical equipment and learn a variety of skills."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LEADER@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "If your Ruler [hyperlink,GLOBAL.RulerVoidConcept]falls[/hyperlink] in combat, they will return to your {GLOBAL.ThroneCityConcept.Hyperlink} after a short time."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LEADER@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitRuler/]Rulers in Battle"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LOW_MORALE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} has [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LowMoraleConcept]Low Morale[/hyperlink], because the tide of battle is turning against it. Units with low morale might {GLOBAL.FumbleConcept} attacks, while high morale can lead to [hyperlink,GLOBAL.CriticalHitConcept]Critical Attacks[/hyperlink]."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LOW_MORALE@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "If a unit's morale drops too low, it will start {GLOBAL.RoutingConcept.Hyperlink} and flee the battlefield."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@LOW_MORALE@TITLE"
msgstr "Unit Morale"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@MAGIC_FIGHTER_UNITS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Magic Fighter {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, a front line melee fighter. It specializes in {GLOBAL.MagicConcept.Hyperlink} attacks, making it ideal for damaging units with high {GLOBAL.DefenseConcept.Hyperlink} like Shield Units."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@MAGIC_FIGHTER_UNITS@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitMagicFighter/]Magic Fighter Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@POLEARM_UNIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Polearm {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, a front line melee fighter. With its {GLOBAL.FirstStrikeConcept} and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ChargeConcept]Charge[/hyperlink] Resistance abilities, it is perfectly suited for absorbing enemy {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} attacks."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@POLEARM_UNIT@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitPolearm/]Polearm Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@RANGED_UNIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Ranged {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, which excels at dealing physical damage from a distance. It is vulnerable to {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} attacks and should be kept in the back line."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@RANGED_UNIT@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitRanged/]Ranged Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@RETALIATION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} just got hit by a {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink}. This happens when a {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} unit is struck from within its Zone of Control."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@RETALIATION@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "A unit has a limited number of <<m:{GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink}>> each turn, shown by red marks under its banner."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@RETALIATION@TITLE"
msgstr "Retaliation"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SCOUT_UNIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Scout {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, which is weak and best kept out of battle. If forced to fight, its high speed and ranged attacks make it a good unit for {GLOBAL.FlankingConcept}."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SCOUT_UNIT@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitScout/]Scout Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SHIELD_UNIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Shield {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, a front line {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} fighter. When entering {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept}, it grants a bonus to adjacent allies, protecting them against physical damage."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SHIELD_UNIT@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitShield/]Shield Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SHOCK_UNITS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Shock {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, a powerful melee fighter specializing in high-damage <<m:{GLOBAL.ChargeConcept}>>. Its attacks can cancel {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept}, which makes it strong against Shield Units and Support Units."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SHOCK_UNITS@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitShock/]Shock Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SKIRMISHER_UNIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Skirmisher {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, which is flexible and uses both ranged and {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept} attacks. With its high speed and Slippery ability, it's the perfect unit for hit-and-run attacks."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SKIRMISHER_UNIT@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitSkirmisher/]Skirmisher Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SPELL_CASTING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Your Spells are now ready to be cast! Spells can have a variety of powerful effects and can turn the tide of battle when used properly."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SPELL_CASTING@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "Spells are unavailable in the first turn of combat, and require {GLOBAL.ManaConcept.Hyperlink} and <<m:{GLOBAL.CombatCastingPointConcept.Hyperlink}>> to use."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SPELL_CASTING@TITLE"
msgstr "Spell Casting"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SUPPORT_UNITS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This is a Support {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}, which can use magical abilities to heal and strengthen its allies."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SUPPORT_UNITS@INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "When entering {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink}, it grants a bonus to adjacent allies, protecting them against magical attacks."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@SUPPORT_UNITS@TITLE"
msgstr "[unitSupport/]Support Units"

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ZONE_OF_CONTORL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Your {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} is in an enemy's Zone of Control. When a unit moves into an enemy's zone of control, it becomes temporarily pinned and cannot move for the rest of the turn."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ZONE_OF_CONTORL@DESCRIPTION_SECONDARY"
msgstr "Moving out of a Zone of Control can trigger an {GLOBAL.OpportunityAttackConcept}.[br/][br/]While in an enemy Zone of Control, many ranged and magical abilities will be unavailable."

msgid "COMBAT_TUTORIAL@ZONE_OF_CONTORL@TITLE"
msgstr "Zone Of Control"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACCURACY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Accuracy is the likelihood of attacks landing successfully. If the attack does not land, it misses or grazes the target.[bulletlist][bullet/]Grazes deal half damage.[bullet/]Misses deal no damage.[bullet/]Misses can hit random adjacent units next to the target.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACCURACY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AccuracyConcept][accuracy/] Accuracy[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACCURACY@NAME"
msgstr "[accuracy/]Accuracy"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> use Action Points to attack and use abilities.[bullet/]Units get 3 Action Points per {GLOBAL.TurnConcept}, and can use up to 2 of them to move.[/bulletlist][br/][br/]Abilities use action points in different ways:[bulletlist][bullet/][singleuseaction/] {LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_SINGLE}[bullet/][repeatingaction/] {LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_REPEATING}[bullet/][fullaction/]{LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FULL}[bullet/][freeaction/] {LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FREE}[bullet/][leaveoneaction/] {LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_LEAVE_ONE}[bullet/][fullactioncontinue/] {LOC.CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FULL_ACTION_CONTINUE}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FREE"
msgstr "Ability costs 0 action points."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FULL"
msgstr "Ability costs 3 action points. The unit's turn ends afterwards."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_FULL_ACTION_CONTINUE"
msgstr "Ability requires 3 action points. The unit retains 1 action point afterwards."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_LEAVE_ONE"
msgstr "Ability costs 0 action points. The unit retains 1 action point afterwards."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_REPEATING"
msgstr "Ability triggers once per remaining action point. The unit's turn ends afterwards."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@DESCRIPTION_SINGLE"
msgstr "Ability costs a single action point. The unit's turn ends afterwards."

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ActionPointConcept]Action Point[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ACTION_POINTS@NAME"
msgstr "Action Point"

msgid "CONCEPT@BASE_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A base attack is a normal attack that a unit can usually use every turn in combat.[br/][br/]Some <<m:{GLOBAL.UnitEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink}>> only affect a unit's base attacks."

msgid "CONCEPT@BASE_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.BaseAbilityConcept]Base[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@BASE_ABILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Base Attack"

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damageBlight/] Blight Damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_DAMAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[damageBlight/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.BlightDamageConcept]Blight Damage[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Blight Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Blight Protection reduces {GLOBAL.BlightDamageConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defenseblight/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.BlightResistanceConcept]Blight Protection[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@BLIGHT_RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Blight Protection"

msgid "CONCEPT@CASUALTIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When a {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} sustains damage, members of the unit are lost.[br/][br/]Each member lost lowers the damage output of the unit proportionally. The chance for the unit to apply <<m:{GLOBAL.NegativeStatusEffectConcept.Hyperlink}>> is also reduced.[br/][br/]A {GLOBAL.LeaderConcept.Hyperlink} or {GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink} unit and large monsters only have a single member and are not affected by this rule."

msgid "CONCEPT@CASUALTIES@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CasualtyConcept]Casualty[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CASUALTIES@NAME"
msgstr "Casualty"

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A Charge attack:[bulletlist][bullet/]Gains extra damage per hex traveled, up to {GLOBAL.ChargeHexes} hexes.[bullet/]Cancels {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Removes {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/][br/]These effects are negated by {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.CHARGE_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink}, unless the attack is a {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.HEAVYMELEESTRIKE.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ChargeConcept]Charge[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE@NAME"
msgstr "Charge"

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE_HEAVY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A Heavy Charge attack:[bulletlist]{LOC.CONCEPT@CHARGE_SHARED}[bullet/]Heavy Charges ignore {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.CHARGE_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE_NORMAL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A Charge attack:[bulletlist]{LOC.CONCEPT@CHARGE_SHARED}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CHARGE_SHARED"
msgstr "[bullet/]Gains {CHARGE_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER>ResolvedDamageMultiplier}% damage per hex traveled, up to {GLOBAL.ChargeHexes} hexes.[bullet/]Cancels {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Removes {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@COMBAT_SPEED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]Combat Speed represents how far a unit can move within a {GLOBAL.TurnConcept} in {GLOBAL.CombatConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Each hex in combat costs {amount} point to traverse.[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SlowingConcept.Hyperlink} terrain costs {amount2} points to traverse.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@COMBAT_SPEED@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[combatspeed/][hyperlink,GLOBAL.CombatSpeedConcept]{LOC.CONCEPT@COMBAT_SPEED@NAME}[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@COMBAT_SPEED@NAME"
msgstr "Combat Speed"

msgid "CONCEPT@CONTROL_LOSS_IMMUNITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Immune to effects that make you lose control of a unit, such as {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.BERSERK.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DOMINATED.Hyperlink}.[br/]Also grants immunity to being {GLOBAL.CapturedConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@CONTROL_LOSS_IMMUNITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ControlLossImmunityConcept]Control Loss Immunity[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CONTROL_LOSS_IMMUNITY@NAME"
msgstr "Control Loss Immunity"

msgid "CONCEPT@CRITICAL_HIT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]If a unit's attack is a Critical Hit, its damage is increased by {damage}.[bullet/]Critical Hits are usually caused by high {GLOBAL.UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Critical Hit chance can never be higher than an attack's chance to hit.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CRITICAL_HIT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CriticalHitConcept]Critical Hit[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CRITICAL_HIT@NAME"
msgstr "Critical Hit"

msgid "CONCEPT@CRITICAL_HIT_CHANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CriticalHitConcept][crit/]Critical Hit Chance[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@CRITICAL_HIT_CHANCE@NAME"
msgstr "[crit/]Critical Hit Chance"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEBUFF_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "An ability that attempts to inflict a {GLOBAL.NegativeStatusEffectConcept.Hyperlink} on an enemy without directly dealing damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@DEBUFF_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DebuffConcept]Debuff[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Defense reduces damage from {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.RangedConcept.Hyperlink} attacks."

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defense/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DefenseConcept]Defense[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE@NAME"
msgstr "Defense"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE_MODE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Defense Mode is a {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} ability. When in Defense Mode, a unit:[bulletlist][bullet/]Extends its {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink} to all adjacent hexes.[bullet/]Gains {defense} {GLOBAL.DefenseConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Gains {resistance} {GLOBAL.ResistanceConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Is immune to {GLOBAL.FlankingConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE_MODE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept]Defense Mode[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@DEFENSE_MODE@NAME"
msgstr "Defense Mode"

msgid "CONCEPT@ENGAGED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "While within an enemy's {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink}, a unit is Engaged in Melee and cannot use most ranged attacks or magical abilities."

msgid "CONCEPT@ENGAGED@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EngagedInMeleeConcept]Engaged in Melee[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ENGAGED@NAME"
msgstr "Engaged in Melee"

msgid "CONCEPT@ETHEREAL_IMMUNITY"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.BLEEDING.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DISEASED.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.IMMOBILIZED.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.POISONED.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@EVASION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Increases chance of {GLOBAL.RangedConcept.Hyperlink} and ranged {GLOBAL.MagicConcept.Hyperlink} attacks missing."

msgid "CONCEPT@EVASION@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EvasionConcept]Evasion[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@EVASION@NAME"
msgstr "Evasion"

msgid "CONCEPT@EXPERIENCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Experience points are earned by units to allow them to reach higher ranks, improving their abilities.[br/][br/]Units earn experience from winning battles. They also earn a small amount each turn on the world map."

msgid "CONCEPT@EXPERIENCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ExperienceConcept][xp/] Experience[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damageFire/] Fire Damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_DAMAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[damageFire/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FireDamageConcept]Fire Damage[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Fire Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_LIGHTNING_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Arcfire Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_LIGHTNING_FROST_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Cosmic Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Fire Protection reduces {GLOBAL.FireDamageConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defensefire/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FireResistanceConcept]Fire Protection[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Fire Protection"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRE_SPIRIT_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Radiant Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRST_STRIKE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When attacked, a unit with First Strike will use a {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink} to attack first."

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRST_STRIKE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FirstStrikeConcept]First Strike[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FIRST_STRIKE@NAME"
msgstr "First Strike"

msgid "CONCEPT@FLANKING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Flanking attacks are triggered by attacking a target from behind or from the side.[bulletlist][bullet/]Flanking attacks deal {damage} damage.[bullet/]Units in {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink} cannot be flanked.[bullet/]If a unit starts its turn in an enemy's {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink}, then it cannot flank it in that turn.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FLANKING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FlankingConcept][flank/] Flanking[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FLANKING@NAME"
msgstr "[flank/] Flanking"

msgid "CONCEPT@FORTIFIED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Can only be damaged by abilities or spells that have {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DEMOLISHER.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@FORTIFIED@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FortifiedConcept]Fortified[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FORTIFIED@NAME"
msgstr "Fortified"

msgid "CONCEPT@FROEST_RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Frost Protection"

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_BLIGHT_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Death Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damageFrost/] Frost Damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_DAMAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[damageFrost/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FrostDamageConcept]Frost Damage[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Frost Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Frost Protection reduces {GLOBAL.FrostDamageConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@FROST_RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defensefrost/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FrostResistanceConcept]Frost Protection[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FUMBLE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]If a unit's attack is a Fumble:[bulletlist][bullet/]A hit becomes a Graze, dealing half damage.[bullet/]A graze becomes a miss.[/bulletlist][bullet/]Fumbles are usually caused by low {GLOBAL.UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FUMBLE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FumbleConcept]Fumble[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@FUMBLE@NAME"
msgstr "Fumble"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@AMBITION@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Ambitions"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@AMBITIONS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Each {GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink} has an Ambition, which sets goals for them to complete and gain {GLOBAL.RenownConcept.Hyperlink}. Each includes a Minor Ambition, which can be repeated any number of times, and a Major Ambition, which can only be completed once.[br/][br/]Completing these ambitions grants {GLOBAL.RenownConcept.Hyperlink}, while completing the Major Ambition additionally grants a unique hero property.[br/][br/]A hero's Ambition may be changed through an event should that hero fail to complete their goals in a set period of time."

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@AMBITIONS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AmbitionConcept]Ambition[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@AMBITIONS@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Ambitions"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@CLASS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Each {GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink} has a Class, chosen during creation. Each class lets the hero specialize in particular roles and often supports two general variations on that role.[br/][br/]Hero Classes:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassDefender.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassWarrior.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassMage.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassRitualist.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassRanger.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassDeathKnight.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.HeroClassSpellblade.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@CLASS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClass]Hero Class[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@CLASS@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Class"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DEDICATION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "At certain levels, heroes gain the ability to choose Signature skills. For <<m:{GLOBAL.MortalChampionConcept.Hyperlink}>>, <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingConcept.Hyperlink}>>, and Dragon Lords, these take the form of Affinity Dedications.[br/][br/]Each tier of Affinity dedication becomes available based on the <<m:{GLOBAL.AffinityConcept.Hyperlink}>> of your empire and your hero's level:[br/][bulletlist][bullet/]Initiate - Requires 1 affinity point and a level 4 Hero.[bullet/]Adept - Requires 4 affinity points and a level 8 Hero.[bullet/]Master - Requires 6 affinity points and a level 12 Hero. [bullet/]Paragon - Requires 8 affinity points and a level 16 Hero.[/bulletlist][br/][br/][br/]These Dedications grant a benefit of their own and unlock new Hero Skills.[br/][br/]Some Hero types such as Eldritch Sovereigns have special Signature Skills that are not related to affinity."

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DEDICATION@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroDedication]Hero Signature Skills[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DEDICATION@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Signature Skills"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DESTINY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Each Hero has a Destiny, which sets goals for the hero to complete to gain {GLOBAL.RenownConcept.Hyperlink}. Each Destiny has a Minor Ambition, which can be repeated any number of times, and a Major Ambition, which can only be completed once.[br/][br/]Completing Ambitions grants {GLOBAL.RenownConcept.Hyperlink}, and completing Major Ambitions grants a unique hero property as well.[br/][br/]A Hero's destiny may be changed through an event should that hero fail to complete its ambitions for a set period of time."

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DESTINY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DestinyConcept]Destiny[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@DESTINY@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Destiny"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@ORIGIN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Origin is determined by the type of hero made during faction creation; for most randomly encountered <<m:{GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink}>> this will be <<m:{GLOBAL.MortalChampionConcept.Hyperlink}>>.[br/][br/]This is where skills unique to those types are found, such as breath attacks for Dragon Lords or spell enchantments for <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@ORIGIN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroOrigin]Hero Origin[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@ORIGIN@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Origin"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@RENOWN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Heroes gain Renown as they complete the goals associated with their {GLOBAL.AmbitionConcept.Hyperlink}. Gaining enough renown increases their Renown Level, which increases the bonuses their [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GovernorConcept]Governed City[/hyperlink] gains from the hero's Governance trait.[br/]Additionally, renown levels grant units in the hero's army additional morale and reduce the chance of losing units when {GLOBAL.RoutingConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@RENOWN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[renown/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.RenownConcept]Renown[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HEROES@RENOWN@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Renown"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEATH_KNIGHT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEATH_KNIGHT@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.GreatWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.OneHandedWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.ShieldConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.FistWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PolearmWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SkirmishingWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEATH_KNIGHT@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that specializes in high damage {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept.Hyperlink} attacks, backed up by <<m:{GLOBAL.DebuffConcept.Hyperlink}>> and summoned {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.UNDEAD.Hyperlink} units."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEATH_KNIGHT@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classDeathknight/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassDeathKnight]Death Knight[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEATH_KNIGHT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassDeathKnight]Hero Class: Death Knight[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEFENDER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEFENDER@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.OneHandedWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.ShieldConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.FistWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PolearmWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SkirmishingWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEFENDER@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that specializes in defending its allies, survivability, and retaliation."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEFENDER@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classDefender/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassDefender]Defender[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@DEFENDER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassDefender]Hero Class: Defender[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@MAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@MAGE@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicOrbWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicStaffWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.EldritchRelicWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@MAGE@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "Elementalists are magical damage dealers setting up attacks or delivering the killing blow with powerful Elemental abilities.[br/]Each Elementalist hero chooses a discipline which determines the element of their abilities."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@MAGE@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classMage/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassMage]Elementalist[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@MAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassMage]Hero Class: Elementalist[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RANGER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RANGER@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.RangedWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SkirmishingWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RANGER@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that specializes in ranged damage, skirmishing, and disrupting enemies."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RANGER@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classRanger/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassRanger]Ranger[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RANGER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassRanger]Hero Class: Ranger[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RITUALIST@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RITUALIST@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicOrbWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicStaffWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.EldritchRelicWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RITUALIST@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that specializes in support through healing and buffs."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RITUALIST@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classRitualist/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassRitualist]Ritualist[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@RITUALIST@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassRitualist]Hero Class: Ritualist[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@SPELLBLADE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@SPELLBLADE@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.GreatWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.OneHandedWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.ShieldConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.FistWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PolearmWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SkirmishingWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@SPELLBLADE@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that uses both {GLOBAL.MeleeConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.MagicConcept.Hyperlink} attacks to deal magic damage from a distance and physical damage when the enemy gets close."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@SPELLBLADE@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classSpellblade/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassSpellblade]Spellblade[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@SPELLBLADE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassSpellblade]Hero Class: Spellblade[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARLOCK@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARLOCK@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicOrbWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.MagicStaffWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.EldritchRelicWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARLOCK@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "Warlocks are debuff and undeath experts, using powerful debuffs and empowering undead summons they raise during battle."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARLOCK@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classWarlock/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassWarlock]Warlock[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARLOCK@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassWarlock]Hero Class: Warlock[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARRIOR@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "{LOC.CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARRIOR@DESCRIPTION_SHORT}[br/][br/]Compatible weapons:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.GreatWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.OneHandedWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.ShieldConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.FistWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PolearmWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.SkirmishingWeaponConcept.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARRIOR@DESCRIPTION_SHORT"
msgstr "A Hero Class that specializes in charge attacks, dealing damage, and gaining strength through fighting."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARRIOR@GAMEPLAY_HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[classWarrior/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassWarrior]Warrior[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_CLASS@WARRIOR@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroClassWarrior]Hero Class: Warrior[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_ADEPT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Adept skills are unlocked by acquiring {amount} other skills in the same category."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_ADEPT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AdeptHeroSkill]Adept Hero Skill[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_EXPERT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Expert skills are unlocked by acquiring {amount} other skills in the same category."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_EXPERT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ExpertHeroSkill]Expert Hero Skill[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_MASTER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Master skills are unlocked by acquiring {amount} other skills in the same category."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_MASTER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MasterHeroSkill]Master Hero Skill[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_NOVICE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A basic hero skill."

msgid "CONCEPT@HERO_SKILL_NOVICE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NoviceHeroSkill]Novice Hero Skill[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HIGHMORALE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HighMoraleConcept]High Morale[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HITPOINTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]Hit Points represent the amount of damage a {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} can sustain before it dies.[bullet/]Most units will take <<m:{GLOBAL.CasualtyConcept.Hyperlink}>> as their Hit Points drop.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HITPOINTS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HitPointConcept]{LOC.CONCEPT@HITPOINTS@NAME}[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@HITPOINTS@NAME"
msgstr "[hp/] Hit Point"

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damageLightning/] Lightning Damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_DAMAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[damageLightning/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LightningDamageConcept]Lightning Damage[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Lightning Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Lightning Protection reduces {GLOBAL.LightningDamageConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defenselightning/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LightningResistanceConcept]Lightning Protection[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@LIGHTNING_RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Lightning Protection"

msgid "CONCEPT@LINE_OF_SIGHT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Most ranged attacks need Line of Sight to target an enemy.[bulletlist][bullet/]If obstacles or other <<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> are between the attacker and the target, the target becomes {GLOBAL.ObscuredConcept.Hyperlink}, reducing {GLOBAL.AccuracyConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Units adjacent to the attacker do not cause a target to be {GLOBAL.ObscuredConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@LINE_OF_SIGHT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LineOfSightConcept]Line of Sight[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@LINE_OF_SIGHT@NAME"
msgstr "Line of Sight"

msgid "CONCEPT@LOWMORALE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LowMoraleConcept]Low Morale[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MAGIC_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Magic Attacks are attacks performed with magical implements such as orbs and staves.[br/][br/]Many of the special attacks that creatures have, such as dragon's breath, are also considered Magic attacks.[br/][br/]Magic attacks are resisted by {GLOBAL.ResistanceConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@MAGIC_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MagicConcept]Magic[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MAGIC_ABILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Magic"

msgid "CONCEPT@MELEE_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Melee attacks are short ranged attacks performed with weapons such as swords, spears, claws and teeth.[br/][br/]They mostly do {GLOBAL.PhysicalDamageConcept.Hyperlink} and are resisted by {GLOBAL.DefenseConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@MELEE_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MeleeConcept]Melee[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MELEE_ABILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Melee"

msgid "CONCEPT@MORALE@SUBTITLE"
msgstr "{minvalue} to {maxvalue} {GLOBAL.UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOUNT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Mounts can be equipped by <<m:{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.HERO.Hyperlink}>> in the relevant slot.[br/]They generally grant {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.FAST_MOVEMENT.Hyperlink} and a small increase in <<m:{GLOBAL.HitPointConcept.Hyperlink}>>.[br/]Certain powerful weapons cannot be wielded while mounted.[br/]The mount that the {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.HERO.Hyperlink} starts with depends on their race and any form traits that race may have."

msgid "CONCEPT@MOUNT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HeroMountConcept]Hero Mount[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOUNT@NAME"
msgstr "Hero Mount"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVEMENT_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "An ability that moves the unit using it to another location.[br/][br/]Cannot be used by units that are {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.IMMOBILIZED.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVEMENT_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MovementAbilityConcept]Movement[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVEMENT_ABILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Movement Ability"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVE_POINTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]Move Points represent how far a unit can move within a {GLOBAL.TurnConcept} on the {GLOBAL.WorldMapConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Normal terrain costs {amount1} Move Points to traverse.[bullet/]Sometimes the Move Point cost of terrain can be reduced, such as when moving through your {GLOBAL.DomainConcept.Hyperlink}, but it can never be reduced below {amount2} Move Points.[bullet/]In {GLOBAL.CombatConcept.Hyperlink} Move Points are not used, {GLOBAL.CombatSpeedConcept.Hyperlink} is used instead.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVE_POINTS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[movementgeneral/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MovePointConcept]Move Point[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@MOVE_POINTS@NAME"
msgstr "[movementgeneral/] Move Point"

msgid "CONCEPT@NEGATIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A negative status effect is a temporary condition that weakens a unit in some way. They are often applied by <<{GLOBAL.DebuffSpellConcept.Hyperlink}>> and {GLOBAL.DebuffConcept.Hyperlink} abilities.[br/][br/]Examples include:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SUNDERED_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.POISONED.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DOMINATED.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.DECAYING.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist][br/][br/]All cultures have a unit ability or spell that can remove negative status effects.[br/][br/]Additionally, some negative status effects have [hyperlink,GLOBAL.OpposingStatusEffectsConcept]counters[/hyperlink]—for example, {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.POISONED.Hyperlink} can be removed by applying {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REGENERATION.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@NEGATIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NegativeStatusEffectConcept]Negative Status Effect[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@NEGATIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@NAME"
msgstr "Negative Status Effect"

msgid "CONCEPT@NEUTRALMORALE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NeutralMoraleConcept]Neutral Morale[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@NO_REFRESH@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Abilities marked with \"Can't be refreshed\" cannot have their cooldowns and \"once per battle\" status reset in battle by special abilities such as {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.WEAVER.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@NO_REFRESH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NoRefreshConcept]Can't be refreshed[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@NO_REFRESH@NAME"
msgstr "Non-Refreshable Abilities"

msgid "CONCEPT@OBSCURED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When a target is Obscured, it becomes {chance}% harder to hit with ranged attacks."

msgid "CONCEPT@OBSCURED@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ObscuredConcept]Obscured[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@OBSCURED@NAME"
msgstr "Obscured"

msgid "CONCEPT@ONE_OF_CONTROL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]A unit's Zone of Control is the three hexes in front of it.[bullet/]The Zone of Control blocks enemy movement and determines where the unit can perform a {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Going into {GLOBAL.DefenseModeConcept.Hyperlink} extends the Zone of Control to all adjacent hexes.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@OPPERTUNITY_ATTACK@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Opportunity Attacks are a special type of {GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept.Hyperlink} that are triggered when an enemy unit leaves the {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@OPPERTUNITY_ATTACK@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.OpportunityAttackConcept]Opportunity Attack[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@OPPERTUNITY_ATTACK@NAME"
msgstr "Opportunity Attack"

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damagePhysical/] Physical Damage."

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_DAMAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[damagePhysical/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.PhysicalDamageConcept]Physical Damage[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_DAMAGE@NAME"
msgstr "Physical Damage"

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Physical Protection reduces {GLOBAL.PhysicalDamageConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[defensephysical/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.PhysicalResistanceConcept]Physical Protection[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@PHYSICAL_RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Physical Protection"

msgid "CONCEPT@POSITIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A positive status effect is a temporary condition that strengthens a unit in some way. They are often applied by <<m:{GLOBAL.BuffSpellConcept.Hyperlink}>> and {GLOBAL.SupportConcept.Hyperlink} abilities.[br/][br/]Examples include:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.BOLSTERED_RESISTANCE.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REGENERATION.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.HASTENED.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.STEADFAST.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist][br/][br/]Certain rare unit abilities and spells can remove positive status effects.[br/][br/]Additionally, some positive status effects have [hyperlink,GLOBAL.OpposingStatusEffectsConcept]counters[/hyperlink]—for example, {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.REGENERATION.Hyperlink} can be removed by applying {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.POISONED.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@POSITIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.PositiveStatusEffectConcept]Positive Status Effect[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@POSITIVE_STATUS_EFFECT@NAME"
msgstr "Positive Status Effect"

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Range refers to the maximum number of hexes away from a unit that an ability can target.[br/]Using attacks on a target at maximum range will often incur an {GLOBAL.AccuracyConcept.Hyperlink} penalty."

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RangeConcept][range/]Range[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGE@NAME"
msgstr "[range/]Range"

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGED_ABILITY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Missile attacks are medium to long ranged attacks performed with weapons such as bows or throwing knives.[br/][br/]They mostly do {GLOBAL.PhysicalDamageConcept.Hyperlink} and are resisted by {GLOBAL.DefenseConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGED_ABILITY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RangedConcept]Missile[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RANGED_ABILITY@NAME"
msgstr "Missile"

msgid "CONCEPT@RESISTANCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Resistance reduces damage from {GLOBAL.MagicConcept.Hyperlink} attacks and <<m:{GLOBAL.CombatSpellConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "CONCEPT@RESISTANCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[resistance/] [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ResistanceConcept]Resistance[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RESISTANCE@NAME"
msgstr "Resistance"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETALIATION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A Retaliation Attack is an attack triggered by another [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UnitConcept]Unit's[/hyperlink] attacks or movement[bulletlist][bullet/]Melee units can Retaliate once per {GLOBAL.TurnConcept} (by default).[bullet/]Attacking an enemy unit within the {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink} triggers a Retaliation.[bullet/]An enemy unit moving out of the {GLOBAL.ZoneOfControlConcept.Hyperlink} triggers an {GLOBAL.OpportunityAttackConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETALIATION@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RetaliationConcept]Retaliation Attack[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETALIATION@NAME"
msgstr "Retaliation Attack"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETREATING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When a {GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink} moves onto a Retreat Point during {GLOBAL.CombatConcept.Hyperlink}, they will immediately exit the battle. [bulletlist][bullet/]Nearby friendly units will lose morale [morale/].[bullet/]The unit will lose Move Points [movementwalk/] after battle.[bullet/]Retreating your last unit will cause you to lose the battle.[bullet/]If you lose the battle, the unit will either die, or scatter and reappear at one of your cities after a few turns.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETREATING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RetreatingConcept]Retreating[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@RETREATING@NAME"
msgstr "Retreating"

msgid "CONCEPT@ROUTING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RoutingConcept]Routing[/hyperlink]"

msgid "CONCEPT@ROUTING@SUBTITLE"
msgstr "{value} {GLOBAL.UnitMoraleConcept.Hyperlink}"

msgid "CONCEPT@RULER@DESTINY@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Each {GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink} has an Ambition, this sets goals for them to complete and gain {GLOBAL.RenownConcept.Hyperlink}. Each includes a Minor ambition, which can be repeated any number of times, and a Major ambition, which can only be completed once."

msgid "CONCEPT@RULER@DESTINY@NAME"
msgstr "Ruler Ambition"

msgid "CONCEPT@SPIRIT_DAMAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Inflicts [damageSpirit/] Spirit Damage."

