msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_ANON@BIO"
msgstr "A simple old man in appearance, Anon represents [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink] virtues like few others. As a Pacifist, Scholar, and Oracle he presides over the Order of Augurs, ensuring that their divine prophecies are chronicled and debated with great care. His wisdom and patience are renowned even among the Archons' enemies.[br/][br/]The Archon Diviners are the enlightened followers of Anon. They dwell at the Lakes of Sagacity, attending to the Order of Augurs and their divine Observatories. When the starlight leads them away from the blessed shores of Emnora, the Archon Diviners will stand against evil and fight for the fulfillment of their prophecies."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_ANON@NAME"
msgstr "Archon Diviners"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_FREDRIC@BIO"
msgstr "The fate of Fredric is a tragic one: cursed in life by the Lizardfolk and again in death by [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath's[/hyperlink] followers, Fredric and his kin of Archon descendants rose as undead {GLOBAL.RevenantsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, driven by evil. Yet when the seals on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} were shattered, their souls broke free from [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath's[/hyperlink] vile influence.[br/][br/]Since then, Fredric seeks a cure to the Revenant curse, fighting for the right of his people to exist and retain their Archon legacy."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_FREDRIC@NAME"
msgstr "Devout Revenants"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_HYKA@BIO"
msgstr "In life, Hyka-Tha was a Grand Architect, known, respected, and revered. In death, she has risen as the advocate of the Awakened. Upon regaining consciousness, she sought her former allies for guidance and support in her corrupted state... But her prayers were answered with a sword wreathed in flames. Now, she wages war—not for vengeance, but for her kin.[br/][br/]More and more Awakened gather under Hyka-Tha's command. Now that they have regained awareness, they ask themselves: If the living also destroy and consume relentlessly, why are the undead denied the right to exist? And so, the deceased raise their necropolises—and their fallen kin—building an empire for those who once fell."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_HYKA@NAME"
msgstr "The Awakened"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_JULIA@BIO"
msgstr "The last remaining Keeper of Life, Empress Julia stood against Death’s bloody star, defending flawed mortality even when its forces unleashed plagues upon a pristine paradise. She is one of the few remaining ancient immortal elves, uncorrupted by the ages and hardship she has endured. Torn from her family and homeland by [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LithylTrueLoreConcept]Lithyl Nightweaver[/hyperlink], Julia was captured in the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and forced to watch helplessly as [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MerlinLoreConcept]Merlin[/hyperlink] traded his soul for her freedom. Despite it all, she balances life's resilience, allies with the peaceable way of nature, and despises those with vast ambitions and narrow visions.[br/][br/]The Exalted Elves have flocked to Julia like moths to a kind and peaceful flame. Like Julia, they aim to bring peace to ravaged realms, rebuilding them in harmony with nature."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_JULIA@NAME"
msgstr "Exalted Elves"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_KLEDAS@BIO"
msgstr "Kledas once created for the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archons[/hyperlink], uniting nature and megaliths into breathtaking works of art. But his ambition drove him to create a wonder that defied the gods; and for that, he was cast out to suffer the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept]Torment of Shadows[/hyperlink]. Now, Kledas roams the world, searching [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AncientWonderConcept]Wonders[/hyperlink] for remnants of his lost creations, desperate to remember who he was... and what he was capable of.[br/][br/]The Dwarves who follow Kledas are both his worshipers and his pupils. They consider him the ultimate artist, a creator of poetry in timeless forms. Every pupil strives to express their art in an unique way, guided by the teachings of their tormented master."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_KLEDAS@NAME"
msgstr "Virtuous Crafters"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_MALIEL@BIO"
msgstr "When the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} cast their Celestial hosts into war, Archpaladin Maliel steers his heavenly chariot headmost. With cleansing flame he descends on the wicked and with zealous conviction he drills his sacred warriors. He is a Paragon of the Order of Highmen and as such propagates their beliefs across the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]The Highmen are the disciples of an Archon Order with high emphasis on martial prowess. Their history is deeply interwoven with the Human race, who they fostered on many {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Through virtuous lives some of those Humans would then ascend to Archonhood—and become Highmen themselves."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_MALIEL@NAME"
msgstr "Highmen"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_PETRAS@BIO"
msgstr "There have always been people like Petras: those born with such a profound sensitivity to the stars that the constellations themselves emerge upon their flesh. But destiny had something even greater prepared for Petras, and so she awakened the Eye of Prophecies. For she is the Weaver of Fates, the one who mends unraveled destinies and guides the Children of the Stars.[br/][br/]As Oracles read the skies, the Stars' Children read their own skin, following the dictates of their marks as a duty to fulfill. They are guided towards mysterious tasks, whose consequences they do not seek to understand. Yet, some whisper that their Weaver is able to see the threads combine into the greater story called the Tapestry of Destiny."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_PETRAS@NAME"
msgstr "Stars' Children"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_REVENANT@BIO"
msgstr "Once an [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink] Titan, Calioth fell during the Archon war against [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept]Myrrida[/hyperlink]. Recently, eldritch magic brutally tore him from his eternal rest, harnessing his rage against enemies he would once call ally. If any spark of light endures within him, it is long buried beneath the shroud of his dark, decaying flesh.[br/][br/]The Ancient [hyperlink,GLOBAL.RevenantsLoreConcept]Revenants[/hyperlink] were once Archons who fought and fell in the name of their divine purpose. Even in death, their struggle endures, for the very darkness they fought now pulls their strings."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@RACE_REVENANT@NAME"
msgstr "Ancient Revenants"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@LORDS@REVENANT_CITY_NAME"
msgstr "Ashwing^N"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@FOUNTAIN_OF_CREATION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "<<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gain:[bulletlist][bullet/]{income}.[bullet/]A [farm/] Farm in this province grants {income2}.[bullet/]The {combatproperty} {GLOBAL.CombatEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/]A {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} with {amount} <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}>> adjacent to this Landmark gains:[bulletlist][bullet/][farm/] Farms in the domain grant {income3} and {income4}.[bullet/]The {combatproperty} {GLOBAL.CombatEnchantmentConcept.Hyperlink} in the domain.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@FOUNTAIN_OF_CREATION@LORE"
msgstr "\"Like the geysers of lustral water we must sanctify the earth and tend it with providential care. By this truth, we erect fountains upon these torrents and thus, by understanding the labor of His work, we draw closer to the Allfather. For what are these streams, if not the incarnation of the Well of Creation made manifest?\"[br/][br/]— Anon Archon Wizard of Life, On the Paths to Divine Ascent"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@MEGAWONDERS_STRATEGIC@FOUNTAIN_OF_CREATION@NAME"
msgstr "Fountain of Creation"

