msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Land on the Coast of Sordünn and explore the ruins of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the fallen Empire of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]Giant Kings[/hyperlink]. Reclaim the realm from the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and fulfill a Prophecy that will shape the war against {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_02@NAME"
msgstr "Cliffs of Sordünn"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_ITEM_02@ASTRAL_MIND"
msgstr "Mind of Godebald"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_01@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "It was during the time of the Great Umbral War, when the denizens of Urrath swarmed the Worlds Within, that many Godir of Magehaven faltered in their faith. For where were the Archons? Had they been defeated, their bastions consumed by the dark tide they could no longer contain? Or had they judged the Pantheon unworthy, abandoning them to their fate?"

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_01@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Gloomwatch, bound by ancient agreements, refused to speak on the matter. Instead they sent their own emissaries to Magehaven, offering to guide single Godir through the World Gates onto a path towards the Archons.[br/][br/]This is the story of one such Godir and their journey of exaltation."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "At long last, through displays of virtue and endurance, the first Godir set foot on the highest ring of Emnora. The Archon High Council, moved by the recounted tragedies of souls claimed in the Great Umbral War, set aside their reservations and decreed the return of the Archons to Magehaven.[br/][br/]As the Celestial battalions emerged from the World Gates, the Pantheon stood in awe, and the Umbral darkness that had shrouded their minds receded."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_01@DEBRIEFING_01_EVIL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In a flare of Celestial light the Archon High Council banished the wicked Godir, who had intruded in their most hallowed sanctuary, from Emnora. They beheld the powers of the Pantheon, seeing how their absence was giving rise to terrible new enemies. Thus they decreed the return of the Archons to Magehaven.[br/][br/]As the Celestial battalions emerged from the World Gates, the Pantheon stood in awe, yet the most maleficent Godir whispered of the Revenants and divine corruption..."

