msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@BRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "At last the Archons had allied themselves with Magehaven in the war against Urrath—and they brought with them a Prophecy which would prove vital if victory were to be attained: the Prophecy of Anon."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@BRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Divine Myopia; Balance Enchained[br/]Giant Empires Fall; Darkness Reigns;[br/]From Traitor's Blood; Fate's Trail Divides;[br/]Corruption Cleansed, Through Fractured Light;[br/]Divine Guard must Rest; For New Powers to Rise;[br/]Who Weigh the Cost of Mercy; Against a Vengeful Demise."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@BRIEFING_03@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "This Prophecy forbade the Archons from getting involved directly, and thus it fell to the Godir of Magehaven to choose one of their own who they deemed powerful enough to fulfill this vital mission. The Archons would lend their strength by sending their champion—an Elven protégé they had taken beneath their divine wings."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@BRIEFING_04@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Their mission was to liberate the Cliffs of Sordünn—the prophesied fallen realm that was once part of the Giant Empire of Myrrida. This realm was to be reclaimed from the Umbral Abyss and its corrupted Ruler, who was desecrating the lands and its inhabitants through foul magic.[br/]Together the two chosen Godir would unveil truths beyond what the Prophecy of Anon foretold."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_01@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "And thus, the prophesied Godir judged Merlin and banished him to the Astral Void. By choosing revenge, parts of the Prophecy of Anon remained unfulfilled. Perhaps, the Archons had to admit, there was a different interpretation to the prophecy besides destroying that which was corrupted by Urrath. But now the chance to fulfill the Prophecy had passed."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_01_MERLINDEFEATED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "And thus, the prophesied Godir judged Merlin and banished him to the Astral Void. By choosing revenge, parts of the Prophecy of Anon remained unfulfilled. Perhaps, the Archons had to admit, there was a different interpretation to the prophecy besides destroying that which was corrupted by Urrath. But now the chance to fulfill the Prophecy had passed."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_01_MERLINSAVED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "And thus, the prophesied Godir judged Merlin and found him worthy of redemption. By channeling the power of the Endailon the curse of Urrath was broken, and the Prophecy of Anon was fulfilled. Magehaven rejoiced: through the creative power of the Affinities it was not only possible to destroy Urrath's influence, but to restore those fallen to its corruption."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_02@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Julia and Sundren remained, bereft of their friend, mentor, and the chance to strike back at Urrath itself. Perhaps, in time, they would find the answers they sought."

msgid "DLC@ARCHONPROPHECY@STORY_REALM_MISSION_02@DEBRIEFING_02_MERLINSAVED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "With this newfound power of restoration, Archons and Godir finally saw a chance to reclaim what was lost, and to begin turning the tide against Urrath."

