msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@HERO_TITLE_9"
msgstr "Eldritch Captive"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@MERLIN_TITLE"
msgstr "Voidbringer"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@MERLIN_TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@ONERON_TITLE"
msgstr "Loremaster"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@ONERON_TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_ASCENDEDINSECTOID_BIO"
msgstr "Naz'ru isn't the smartest of his people, nor the wisest, or most charismatic. Above all, he is the biggest and the most protective, and among the first to shed the corruption of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Under his rule, the dwellings of the Shadir'ko have evolved into thriving cities.[br/][br/]The Shadir'ko were once mindless thralls under the rule of Lithyl, corrupted by Urrath. Only after ages of neglect were they able to slowly and through much loss find their own identities, which they now viciously defend."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_ASCENDEDINSECTOID_CITYNAME"
msgstr "Xa'rapac^N"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_ASCENDEDINSECTOID_NAME"
msgstr "Shadir'ko"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_INSECTOIDSOVEREIGN@BIO"
msgstr "Ra'cheq was, as he himself proclaims, but an insect, living in the dirt and feeding on scraps. Until one day the sun eclipsed, the stars darkened and the world was embraced by {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Ra'cheq was the first to crawl from under the rubble and he believes that is why he was Chosen to lead his newly awakened people to greatness.[br/][br/]Ra'cheq's followers believe themselves to be the chosen disciples of Urrath, their dark god. They are prone to violence and jealousy, vying for their god's corrupted love without hesitation to betray even their own kin if their High Corruptor demands it."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_INSECTOIDSVEREIGN@NAME"
msgstr "Children of Urrath"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_INSECTOIDWARDEN@BIO"
msgstr "Once, Ryc'Turi was nothing but one drone in the hive-mind of her people, following the orders of their Sovereign Lithyl without question. In her absence, however, Ryc'Turi was the first of her people to take initiative beyond the direct orders she was given. Where this newly-found ambition will lead her, she herself hardly knows.[br/][br/]Born and raised on Tharru'Cath, the Shadac'har know very little beyond oppressive violence and blind loyalty to {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their overlords. Over time, however, they developed the power to communicate with other peoples and started to show an eagerness to build that their former Sovereign would undoubtedly deem mildly concerning."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_INSECTOIDWARDEN@NAME"
msgstr "Shadac'har"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_LITHYL@BIO"
msgstr "Once a powerful Wizard, Lithyl Nightweaver fell to her {GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and became [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept]Lost[/hyperlink], before the dark god {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink} twisted her blind insanity and broken body into something considerably more menacing. After a time of imprisonment wrought upon her by the Elven princess Sundren, Lithyl returns to exact her revenge on her captor, {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, and the entire {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]Not all who wander the Astral Sea are {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Many mortals find themselves lost in its depths, forgotten, with no divine power to save them. Still, some may consider oblivion a more merciful fate than to be found by Lithyl Nightweaver, the Harbinger of Urrath, who extends an eldritch hand and strangles those in her grasp until they are nothing but mindless thralls in her game of corruption."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_LITHYL@NAME"
msgstr "Chosen of Urrath"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_MEANDOR@NAME"
msgstr "Swarming Hammers"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_MERLIN@BIO"
msgstr "As a young human prince, Merlin was chosen by the Archon Gabriel to restore the balance of power on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. The Wizard's Circle, the All-Devourer, the Shadowborn—as a masterful wizard of the cosmos, Merlin protected the people of Athla throughout the Ages even after he had withdrawn from power, exploring large parts of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. At last he was betrayed by his own love, falling into the clutches of Lithyl Nightweaver in a desperate attempt to save Julia of House Inioch from [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath's grasp[/hyperlink]. Now, reshaped into an Eldritch Sovereign through Urrath's vile corruption, all that Merlin desires appears to be for the cosmos to swiftly end so that all suffering and agony of the world may forever be forgotten.[br/][br/]The Umbral Humans are Merlin's instrument of annihilation. They bring oblivion to the realms he treads, as oblivion is what their master desires."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_MERLIN@NAME"
msgstr "Umbral Humans"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_ONERON@BIO"
msgstr "Born as a thrall within the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, O'neron returned his people their freedom when he joined arms with the Wizard Kings of the Second Age on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to destroy the All-Devourer. Since then, he has traveled the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, reaching other realms of free Syron civilizations. Through the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, he rediscovered his history and heritage, forever linked to Athla.[br/][br/]The Gloomwatch Syrons sail the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in search and protection of the {GLOBAL.DreamersLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They are gifted in the arcane and have developed high versatility when resisting the fell reach of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and its {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_ONERON@NAME"
msgstr "Gloomwatch Syrons"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_WIZARDSYRON_BIO"
msgstr "As a direct descendant of the first Syrons, Aeri grew up in reverence of the history of the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Yet, as her talents as a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept]Wizard[/hyperlink] grew, her {GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept.Hyperlink} made her question her assigned burden as a cosmic protector. Instead, she decided to offer sanctuary to those who choose simpler lives... Though in the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, that in itself is a challenge.[br/][br/]The Free Syrons consist mainly of veterans, and people who declined the duty and honor of the Gloomwatch in favor of a calmer life on the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Yet, when threatened, they will stand their ground next to any other battle-hardened warrior."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@RACE_WIZARDSYRON_NAME"
msgstr "Free Syrons"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@SUNDREN_TITLE"
msgstr "Shadow Walker"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@LORDS@SUNDREN_TITLE@GENDER"
msgstr "^f"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MARKERS_TACTICAL@SPLITTERLING_NEST@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Every {turn} <<m:{GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}>>, a {GLOBAL.UNITS.SPLITTERLING.Hyperlink} is summoned on the defending side adjacent to this obstacle."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MARKERS_TACTICAL@SPLITTERLING_NEST@NAME"
msgstr "Splitterling Nest"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGN_CUSTOMIZATION1_NAME"
msgstr "Eldritch Guardian Head"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGN_CUSTOMIZATION2_NAME"
msgstr "Eldritch Ogre Head"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGN_CUSTOMIZATION3_NAME"
msgstr "Eldritch Fractured Evoker Head"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@OBJECTIVE_HOUSE_CONQUERED@NAME"
msgstr "Umbral Dwelling Conquered"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@OBJECTIVE_HOUSE_VASSALIZED@NAME"
msgstr "Pact with Umbral Dwelling"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@PROGRESSION_ITEM@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGN_APPEARANCE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Unlocks a new appearance item for your Eldritch Sovereign rulers to use."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_FEY_INVASION@NAME_01"
msgstr "Cióghan Ruins"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@NAME1"
msgstr "Shadowgrip"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@NAME2"
msgstr "Umbranis"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@NAME3"
msgstr "The Darklands"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@NAME4"
msgstr "Longshade"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@NAME5"
msgstr "The Precipice"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@SUBTITLE"
msgstr "Hollow winds howl where laughter once resounded, and shadows herald death where once they followed life."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@REALM_SHADOWREALM@TEMPLATE_NAME"
msgstr "Umbral Abyss"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@TRAIT_SHADOW_ENABLED@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The {GLOBAL.UmbralAbyssConcept.Hyperlink} creeps over this realm, opening gates to an eldritch dimension and its invading horrors:[bulletlist][bullet/]An additional map layer called the Umbral Abyss is added, which can be reached through Umbral Gates.[bullet/]Enter the Umbral Abyss for forbidden treasures—at a great risk![bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.InfestationConcept.Hyperlink}>> and <<m:{GLOBAL.DwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> from the Umbral Abyss will creep into the Surface and Underground, spreading {GLOBAL.GloomTerrainConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> in Gloom Terrain will suffer from {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@TRAIT_SHADOW_ENABLED@NAME"
msgstr "Umbral Abyss"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@TRAIT_SHADOW_ENABLED_MINOR@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A lesser version of the {GLOBAL.UmbralAbyssConcept.Hyperlink}:[bulletlist][bullet/]No Umbral <<m:{GLOBAL.DwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> present.[bullet/]Reduced amount of Umbral islands with <<m:{GLOBAL.InfestationConcept.Hyperlink}>>.[bullet/]Reduced amount of Umbral islands and Umbral Gates overall.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@META_EMPIRE@TRAIT_SHADOW_ENABLED_MINOR@NAME"
msgstr "Subdued Umbral Abyss"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINORFACTIONS_WORLD@THRALL_RACE@BENEFIT1"
msgstr "This race are designated thralls for all <<m:{GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> in the realm and will primarily appear in the {GLOBAL.UmbralAbyssConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINORFACTIONS_WORLD@THRALL_RACE@BIO_1"
msgstr "It is said that the Umbral Thralls were once a free civilization governed by a benevolent hivemind. Yet through [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath's eldritch lashes[/hyperlink], the minds of the Umbral Thralls became enchained, and their hive was twisted into an instrument of enslavement. As will-less drones they serve as unceasing warriors, laborers, or as a harvest of souls to satiate the hunger of the {GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Their swarm carries the gloom to other realms, so that other free peoples across the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} might share the same terrible fate."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINORFACTIONS_WORLD@THRALL_RACE@DESCRIPTION_1"
msgstr "The {GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink} tolerates you. [br/]Grants the same benefits as {GLOBAL.PTDNeutralConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.OpenBordersConcept.Hyperlink}. [br/][br/]If you assign a {GLOBAL.WhisperingStoneConcept.Hyperlink} and make more sacrifices you may reach an {GLOBAL.EldritchPactConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINORFACTIONS_WORLD@THRALL_RACE@NAME_1"
msgstr "Umbral Thralls"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@ABYSS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "These are the Initiates of the Umbral Abyss, who use otherworldly magic that mutates them with extra limbs. Their pact with the abyss makes their flesh twisted and immune to the Umbral Malady."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@ABYSS@NAME"
msgstr "Initiates of the Umbral Abyss"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@CORRUPTION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "These are the Masters of Corruption, who use twisted magic that defiles and mutates their own. Through these foul practices they can even siphon their enemies' strengths in battle."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@CORRUPTION@NAME"
msgstr "Masters of Corruption"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@FLAME@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "They are the Masters of the Cleansing Flame, who incinerate the battlefield with zeal and vigor to bless the faithful and cleanse the land of corruption."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MINOR_FACTION@UPGRADE_SET@FLAME@NAME"
msgstr "Masters of the Cleansing Flame"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@MOUNT@BEETLE"
msgstr "Giant Beetle Mount^n"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@ADJECTIVE_1"
msgstr "Insectoid^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@ADJECTIVE_2"
msgstr "Carapaced^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@ADJECTIVE_3"
msgstr "Chitinous^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@ADJECTIVE_4"
msgstr "Carapaced^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@NOUN_1"
msgstr "Insects"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@NOUN_2"
msgstr "Insectoids"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_INSECTOID@NOUN_3"
msgstr "Chitins"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_SYRON@ADJECTIVE_1"
msgstr "Syron^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_SYRON@ADJECTIVE_2"
msgstr "Star-Born^a"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NAMES_RACES@FORM_SYRON@NOUN_1"
msgstr "Syrons"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@GOLD_NODE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "These grotesque growths deposit valuable liquid and ore at unnatural speed."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@GOLD_NODE@NAME"
msgstr "Chitinous Growths"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@KNOWLEDGE_NODE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "There is writing in an unknown language on these obsidian giants."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@KNOWLEDGE_NODE@NAME"
msgstr "Monoliths"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@NODES@RUINED_CHITINOUS_NODE@NAME"
msgstr "Ruined Chitinous Growths"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@NODES@RUINED_MONOLITHS_NODE@NAME"
msgstr "Ruined Monoliths"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@NODES@RUINED_VOID_STONES@NAME"
msgstr "Ruined Void Stones"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_INK@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.PvEVassalConcept.Hyperlink}>> give +{amount1} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> with an {GLOBAL.EldritchPactConcept.Hyperlink} give +{amount2}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_INK@NAME"
msgstr "Void Ink"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_STONES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Unique global effect: [bulletlist][bullet/]Gain {allegiance}{GLOBAL.HouseInfluenceConcept.Hyperlink} with discovered <<m:{GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> per {GLOBAL.TurnConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]Allows the forging of misc items that grant immunity to {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink} in the {GLOBAL.ItemForgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_STONES@LORE"
msgstr "\"Levitating stones, smooth as silk, unlike any I encountered on or under the known worlds. Touch one, and the forbidden words of Umbral denizens roll off your tongue. Tap one with a hammer, and its Astral attunement resonates. They seem impossible to split in twain but I suspect they are, in fact, geodes. What treasure is hoarded within?\"[br/][br/]—Fangir Rockborne, Journals from the Second Age: Appendix"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_STONES@NAME"
msgstr "Void Stones"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_STONES_SET_BONUS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "[bulletlist][bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink}>> with an {GLOBAL.EldritchPactConcept.Hyperlink} grant +{amount1} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[bullet/]<<m:{GLOBAL.PvEVassalConcept.Hyperlink}>> grant +{amount2} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}.[/bulletlist][br/][br/]Requires:[bulletlist][bullet/]{amount3} {GLOBAL.STRUCTURES.VOID_STONES.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@NODES_STRATEGIC@VOID_STONES_SET_BONUS@NAME"
msgstr "Void Ink"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@CHITIN_PICKUP@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The discarded and hardened shells of various Umbral Demon creatures. Could be used for construction of armor or buildings, or sold as exotic materials.[br/][br/]May grant a great amount of {GLOBAL.GoldConcept.Hyperlink}, {GLOBAL.UnitProductionConcept.Hyperlink}, or {GLOBAL.StructureProductionConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@CHITIN_PICKUP@NAME"
msgstr "Discarded Chitin"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@SOULS_PICKUP@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Husks of formerly powerful beings, haunting the surrounding area. They could bear dark secrets or be turned into raw power.[br/][br/]May grant a great amount of {GLOBAL.ManaConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink}. If available, also grants {amount} <<m:{GLOBAL.SoulConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@SOULS_PICKUP@NAME"
msgstr "Tormented Souls"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@TOME_PICKUP@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Pages upon pages describing rites, rituals, and signs. And yet only a fragment of a complete {GLOBAL.TomeConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]When picked up, unlocks a single {GLOBAL.SpellConcept.Hyperlink} that you do not have [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ResearchConcept]researched[/hyperlink] yet and are not currently researching."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@PICKUPS_STRATEGIC@TOME_PICKUP@NAME"
msgstr "Tome Fragment"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@BIO"
msgstr "Their vast knowledge earns them power and respect throughout the realms."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@EFFECT1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Unlocking a new Research Skill grants +10 {GLOBAL.HouseInfluenceConcept.Hyperlink} with all <<m:{GLOBAL.IndependentCityConcept.Hyperlink}>> to whom you have assigned a {GLOBAL.DiplomaticTokenConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@EFFECT2@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Unlocking a new {GLOBAL.TomeConcept.Hyperlink} grants +{amount} Relation with all <<m:{GLOBAL.EmpireConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@EFFECT3@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Gain +{amount} {GLOBAL.KnowledgeConcept.Hyperlink} income for each empire you have {GLOBAL.OpenBordersConcept.Hyperlink} with."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@INCOME_MODIFIER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Keepers of Knowledge: Open Borders Treaty"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@LORE"
msgstr "They know knowledge is power, and power demands respect."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@MODIFIER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Keepers of Knowledge: Tome Unlocked"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@KEEPERS_OF_KNOWLEDGE@NAME"
msgstr "Keepers of Knowledge [goodact/]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@BIO"
msgstr "They know the shadows are not to be feared, but to be studied and used."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@EFFECT1@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Start with {GLOBAL.SPECIAL_OPERATIONS.UMBRAL_FLESH.Hyperlink} active."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@EFFECT2@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Cities may build the {GLOBAL.STRUCTURE_UPGRADES.ALTAR_OF_MARCHING_GLOOM.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@EFFECT3@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Your Ruler gains {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.TYRANTS_RETINUE_HERO.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@EFFECT4@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Start with {GLOBAL.SPECIAL_OPERATIONS.GLOOM_WARD.Hyperlink} unlocked."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@LORE"
msgstr "The shadows whisper, and the disciples listen."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@RACETRAITS_WORLD@UMBRAL_DISCIPLES@NAME"
msgstr "Umbral Disciples [evilact/]"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SDIPLOMACY@HOUSE_INFLUENCE_BOOST@DESCRIPTION_UMBRAL"
msgstr "Engage with the {GLOBAL.UmbralDwellingConcept.Hyperlink} to reveal their demands for increasing their {GLOBAL.HouseInfluenceConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWCLIFFS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Jagged rock plunging into depths. The precipice of the abyss.[br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> in Umbral terrain suffer {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWCLIFFS@NAME"
msgstr "Cliff"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWFOREST@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Various otherworldly flora, or are they fauna?[br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> in Umbral terrain suffer {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWFOREST@NAME"
msgstr "Forest"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWLANDS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Gloom terrain is normally only found in the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> except <<m:{GLOBAL.MarauderConcept.Hyperlink}>> within Gloom provinces suffer {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}, and <<m:{GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink}>> suffer {happiness}{GLOBAL.CityStabilityConcept.Hyperlink} for every annexed Gloom {GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink} within their {GLOBAL.DomainConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWLANDS@NAME"
msgstr "Gloom"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWMOUNTAIN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Mountains of madness, spires of doom.[br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> in Umbral terrain suffer {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWMOUNTAIN@NAME"
msgstr "Mountains"

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWPLAINS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Plains covered in darkness, vast and ominous.[br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.UnitConcept.Hyperlink}>> in Umbral terrain suffer {GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.SHADOW_SICKNESS.Hyperlink}."

msgid "DLC@ELDRITCHREALMS@SECTORDEFINITIONS_STRATEGIC@SHADOWPLAINS@NAME"
