msgid "DLC@GIANTKINGS@LORDS@HERO_BIO_1"
msgstr "A proud descendant of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]Giant Kings[/hyperlink] of old, Fjalla carries the responsibility of her royal ancestors on her shoulders. Her father taught her about the beauty of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, and Fjalla vowed to see its glory reborn.[br/][br/]Fjalla's Jordvolk are proud artisans whose ancestry dates back to the empire of Myrrida, where they served Giant King Thrudgelmir before they pledged their loyalty to his daughter. Under the rule of Fjalla, they honed their craft to perfection, and feel confident of bringing the glory of Myrrida to the Realms once more."

msgid "DLC@GIANTKINGS@LORDS@HERO_BIO_2"
msgstr "Like many of his kin, Fflammych was born and raised amidst the rivalry between {GLOBAL.GiantsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. As the guardian of his hearth, Fflammych has seen many a battle and has always protected his kin and people with fire and blood. Recently, however, revelations of greater dangers than Dragons have dimmed the vengeance in his heart. Some say he even dares to question the ancient rivalries.[br/][br/]Fflammych's Hearthkin believe their {GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are forged in the heart of their Giant King, and thus they follow Fflammych with unwavering loyalty. As wielders of the soul-flame, their pyromancers are revered like priests."

msgid "DLC@GIANTKINGS@LORDS@HERO_BIO_3"
msgstr "As a rumored descendant of one of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept]Traitor Kings[/hyperlink], Singaith seems to have inherited her ancestors' obsession with power and immortality. Reclusive and self-centered, she values knowledge over any form of other fleeting relationship as she schemes for the glory of her kin to rise again.[br/][br/]Like their ruler Singaith and the Traitor Kings of old, the Galetoads are obsessed with achieving eternal life. Through the magic of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept]Soul[/hyperlink] and the knowledge of the {GLOBAL.EternalCouncilLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, they hope to make their eternal dream a reality... through any means necessary."

msgid "DLC@GIANTKINGS@LORDS@HERO_BIO_4"
msgstr "Hrímis was a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantsLoreConcept]Giant[/hyperlink] serving the ancient [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]Giant Kings[/hyperlink] until the Giant Empire of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} fell to the combined forces of {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Since then, she has been a recluse and avoids any contact with outsiders unless absolutely necessary. Perhaps the encroaching corruption by the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is one such necessity.[br/][br/]The Kaldbörn are the devoted servants of Hrímis, thriving within the frigid depths of the underground. Much like their Empress, they shun direct conflict, choosing instead to observe from the shadows as great empires crumble."

msgid "DLC@GIANTKINGS@LORDS@HERO_TITLE_1"
msgstr "Giant Queen"

