msgid "DLC@RISEFROMRUIN@LORDS@HERO_TITLE@YLAC@GENDER"
msgstr "^m"

msgid "DLC@RISEFROMRUIN@LORDS@RACE_KE-NAN@BIO"
msgstr "After reclaiming leadership of his tribe on Athla, Ke-nan never ceased his fight against slavery. When the Desert of Kesh was finally freed from the \"old ways,\" the Shatterer of Shackles and his people set out for new worlds. For ages, Ke-nan has wandered across barren realms, freeing those who lived in chains.[br/][br/]The war against the {GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} left a lasting mark on the culture of the Freefolk of Kesh. Embracing magic to empower oneself was seen as an omen of catastrophe; for sooner or later, the thirst for power would corrupt them. In time, these practices became taboo. As the Freefolk of Kesh say: \"Sometimes shackles do not clink—they whisper.\""

msgid "DLC@RISEFROMRUIN@LORDS@RACE_YLAC@BIO"
msgstr "As a child who never belonged, Ylac always wanted to learn more about [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UnmakersLoreConcept]those who should be forgotten[/hyperlink]. Ignoring the legends and laws of his tribe, he entered a {GLOBAL.STRUCTURES.FRACTURED_TOWER.Hyperlink}. When he returned home, Ylac was changed. His eyes glowed with a hollow energy, and his mind hungered to know more. But his tribe saw only a monster in the making; and so they cast him out.[br/][br/]The Cursed Wanderers share the affliction that corrodes their leader, one that has only just begun to take shape. Ylac gathered them with promises of power: the power to uncover the source of their affliction, the power to find their place in the world—or the power to reshape the world to fit their image."

