msgstr "Black Knight"

msgid "DLC@THRONESOFBLOOD@LORDS@RACE_GUINDY@BIO"
msgstr "It is said that the Great Bat was wounded and its blood fell from the sky. When Guindy first drank that vibrant liquid, he felt himself ascend. His senses sharpened, his strength grew unstoppable, and his endurance knew no bounds. For generations he ruled his tribe as a ruthless chieftain, now he rules them as a wise deity—the Apex Predator.[br/][br/]To the Crimson Gazers, vampirism is the natural culmination of their kind. They already hunted the night, devoured their enemies, and showed no mercy. In the wild, you are prey or predator. Nothing else."

msgid "DLC@THRONESOFBLOOD@LORDS@RACE_URSUL@BIO"
msgstr "The Blackrose Baron is the subject of legends and tragic tales. They say his Vampire ascension was never his choice. They whisper that he was bitten in battle, facing [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchvampireLoreConcept]a being as old as the blood-curse[/hyperlink] itself. They say he was shunned like a plague and imprisoned in his own city by the neighboring Dwarven kingdom... And that, consumed by an uncontrollable hunger, he devoured his family and his people.[br/][br/]Legends also claim that the Black Marchers are the descendants of the Dwarves who sealed the Baron’s fate. After generations of thralldom and the bites of their master, they have become perfect vessels, capable of quelling Ursul's thirst for revenge."

msgid "DLC@THRONESOFBLOOD@LORDS@RACE_VARNAS@BIO"
msgstr "The Bathoris name traces back to the ancient Dominion of Rued Drevanya, where Vampire society reached its zenith. Though the glory of that empire has long since faded, the Marquess continues to host the grand balls of old times for those daring enough to attend... And those who fail to keep up with the court intrigues often end up as its appetizer.[br/][br/]To escape the torment of sunlight, Varnas established his court in the underground, accessible only through the family crypt. There he has fashioned a race of servants, feeding Goblins with his own blood and that of bats. Some whisper that the Shrieking Bats are also his creation, though none dare speculate on the manner of their breeding."

msgid "DLC@THRONESOFBLOOD@LORDS@RACE_YMBRIA@BIO"
msgstr "Two ages ago, Ymbria performed a blood ritual that granted her a perverse immortality. Aided by an ancient tome of questionable origin, she sacrificed her entire cult and concocted a potion from their blood. Yet it did not bestow the eternal beauty she craved. Instead, her body remains in a perpetual state of decay, something that can only be rectified by feeding upon the living.[br/][br/]Ymbria has rebuilt her cult under the teachings of the tome's author. He who now whispers profane rites in her mind, He who now calls upon her, demanding to be awakened again. The Cult of the Blood Rite follows their priestess, who obeys the call in hope of attaining true immortality."

