msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AFFINITIES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The six affinities are the cosmic forces that shape and define all that exists. [hyperlink,GLOBAL.OrderConcept]Order[/hyperlink], [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ChaosConcept]Chaos[/hyperlink], [hyperlink,GLOBAL.NatureConcept]Nature[/hyperlink], [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowConcept]Shadow[/hyperlink], [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MateriumConcept]Materium[/hyperlink] and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralConcept]Astral[/hyperlink] are the powers that encompass the cosmos, each vastly different in its domain, applications and nature. When channeling magic, the aspects of these cosmic forces will be invoked.[br/][br/]The {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are dedicated to studying the six affinities in order to harness their powers to the greatest effect. Their findings are inscribed in {GLOBAL.TomeLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, true testaments to the godly ambitions of their authors."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AFFINITIES@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AffinitiesLoreConcept]Affinities[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AFFINITIES@TITLE"
msgstr "Magic Affinities"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ALFRED_ELDERSTONE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AlfredElderstoneLoreConcept]Alfred Elderstone^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ALFRED_ELDERSTONE@NAME"
msgstr "Alfred Elderstone^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ALLFATHER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The \"Allfather\" is one of the names given to a supreme being shrouded in mystery. Worshiped as a force of creation, they are known by many different identities throughout the cosmos. Some say they shaped the mythical [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept]Well of Creation[/hyperlink] while others believe that the being and the Well form a holy duality that cannot be separated.[br/][br/]The {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} have spread the faith of the \"Allfather\" to many [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]Worlds[/hyperlink], the being's manifestation morphing toward the perception of the various races. While the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} claim to be the \"Allfather's\" celestial servants, there are no trustworthy sources that would demonstrate the being's intentions or any will to interfere with the dealings of mortals."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ALLFATHER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept]Allfather[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ALLFATHER@TITLE"
msgstr "Allfather"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ANCIENT_KRAZURA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In ages past, long before the rise of the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} on {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the Ancient Krazura were the sages of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, knowledgeable and gifted in the arcane unlike any others. Their counsel and magecraft was sought by many, above all by the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who grew to depend on the Ancient Krazura during the {GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Together they devised the Vaultsphere, the World Seals and eventually {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, bringing an end to the {GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and largely restoring Archon order on the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]Around that time, however, the Ancient Krazura mysteriously vanished and any record of their civilization and works became lost in the ages to follow. Only after the opening of {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the return of the {GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is their history and heritage being rediscovered."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ANCIENT_KRAZURA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AncientKrazuraLoreConcept]Ancient Krazura[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ANCIENT_KRAZURA@TITLE"
msgstr "Ancient Krazura"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ANON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AnonLoreConcept]Anon[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ANON@NAME"
msgstr "Anon^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARACHNA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArachnaLoreConcept]Arachna^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHONS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Archons believe they were created by the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} himself as the first sentient race, and tasked with advancing his works of creation. Through the ages, they have proudly called themselves the Allfather's divine guardians against evil, protecting new [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]Worlds[/hyperlink] from the dangers of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. However, in recent ages they have withdrawn from many Worlds and only rarely seek contact with the non-celestial races."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHONS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archons[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHONS@TITLE"
msgstr "Archons"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHSIRE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A myth even among Vampires themselves, the Archvampires are said to have been bitten by the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrvatoghLoreConcept]Deathless God[/hyperlink], the very first Vampire to roam the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They are ancient and proud, dismissing the <<m:{GLOBAL.ElderVampireLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> that sprang from their own fangs. Or so it is told in the tales of the Crimson Reign. Yet the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrvatoghLoreConcept]Deathless God[/hyperlink], his dominion and consorts all vanished in the mists of time."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHSIRE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchvampireLoreConcept]Archvampire[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARCHSIRE@TITLE"
msgstr "Archvampire"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARTICA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArticaLoreConcept]Artica^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARVIK@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArvikLoreConcept]Arvik the Dark^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ARVIK@NAME"
msgstr "Arvik the Dark^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASCENDEDINSECTOID@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AscendedInsectoidLoreConcept]Naz'ru Ka'zorak^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASCENDEDINSECTOID@NAME"
msgstr "Naz'ru Ka'zorak^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASC_CHAMPION@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Ascended Champions are mortals who joined the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept]Pantheon of Godir[/hyperlink] at {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} through their mastery of the arcane arts. They bear resemblance to their mortal origins and have a close connection with and understanding of the people they rule."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASC_CHAMPION@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AscendedChampLoreConcept]Ascended Champion[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASC_CHAMPION@TITLE"
msgstr "Ascended Champion"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASGERA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AsgeraLoreConcept]Asgera Spinesplitter^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASGERA@NAME"
msgstr "Asgera Spinesplitter^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Affinity"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_FLOW@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Astral Flows are the magical currents within the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} that connect all worlds and living beings. Where these flows breach the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]material realm[/hyperlink] they consolidate their magic into Mana Nodes. Here, magic users can tap into the flow to power their spells. Powerful beings may enter the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} through these breaches to follow the Astral Flows to other [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]worlds[/hyperlink]."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_FLOW@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept]Astral Flows[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_FLOW@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Flows"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Astral Sea is the primal source of arcane powers, a vast aetherial ocean containing and connecting the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. This ocean ebbs and flows, pushes and pulls, seeps into the material world through Mana Nodes. It contains [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralDwellersLoreConcept]beings of pure magical energy[/hyperlink] such as the Node Serpent and is traversed by the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept]souls of the dead[/hyperlink] on their final journey to {GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]Powerful mages may follow the {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to travel between worlds, but it is a dangerous journey where they may be lured away into the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink} or become a victim of {GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. A much safer method involves the use of <<m:{GLOBAL.WorldGateLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>, which however require great knowledge and skill to be created or used."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept]Astral Sea[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Sea"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_DWELLERS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Though alien to most visitors from the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is not empty or dead. In between its {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, an entire ecosystem thrives, where creatures and plants intertwine with the arcane energy as it ebbs and flows. Natural predators and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept]Monsters[/hyperlink] roam the astral depths, while lone wanderers of the ancient {GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept.Hyperlink} bear rare witness to a once great civilization."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_DWELLERS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralDwellersLoreConcept]Astral Sea Dwellers[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_DWELLERS@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Sea Dwellers"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_MONSTERS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Astral Sea Monsters are denizens of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. These mana-hungry creatures come in a variety of shapes, from the jellyfish like Astral Syphoner to the horrifically tragic {GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They are all designed to thrive in the harsh environment of the Astral Sea, with many leeching life from any traveler caught unaware. However, not all Astral Sea creatures are malevolent, as the gentle {GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are prove."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_MONSTERS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept]Astral Sea Monsters[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_SEA_MONSTERS@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Sea Monsters"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VOID@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Beyond the reach of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} lies the Astral Void, a place where the {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} do not reach, a place of nothingness. A wizard may be banished and cast into the Void, where they drift around until they either manage to find a flow leading them back to a safe place or succumb to the {GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and perish as one of the <<m:{GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VOID@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept]Astral Void[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VOID@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Void"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VORTEX@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Sometimes the {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} converge into astral vortices, paradoxical culminations of magic energy that bend all meaning of time and space. When entered by beings powerful enough to withstand their shearing forces, they may be used to traverse large distances within the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. However, many prefer the use of the much safer—but also rarer—<<m:{GLOBAL.WorldGateLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VORTEX@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralVortexLoreConcept]Astral Vortex[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ASTRAL_VORTEX@TITLE"
msgstr "Astral Vortex"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ATHLA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Athla is one of the oldest {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} with a potent convergence of {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. It is the home to the {GLOBAL.ValleyofWondersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and Inioch's court. Through the ages Athla has played a pivotal role in events that shaped the cosmos, be it as a realm to conquer, a scene of cosmic battles, or the origin of powerful beings. Many known {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} originate from this world."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ATHLA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept]Athla[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ATHLA@TITLE"
msgstr "Athla"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AULDWEALD@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Auldweald is said to be the original homeworld of the First Elves, from where they first traveled to other [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]Worlds[/hyperlink] in the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Many elven songs idolize its lush valleys and evergreen forests, and it is said that all elven {GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} long to return to this world."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AULDWEALD@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AuldwealdLoreConcept]Auldweald[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AULDWEALD@TITLE"
msgstr "Auldweald"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AYA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AyaLoreConcept]Aya the Enlightened^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AYA@NAME"
msgstr "Aya the Enlightened^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AZANYA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AzanyaLoreConcept]Azanya^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@AZANYA@NAME"
msgstr "Azanya^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BHAJIF@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.BhajifLoreConcept]Bhajif Erranstar^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BHAJIF@NAME"
msgstr "Bhajif Erranstar^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BIRCHFOOT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.BirchfootLoreConcept]Birchfoot the Hermit^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BIRCHFOOT@NAME"
msgstr "Birchfoot the Hermit^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BLINT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.BlintUnderdelverLoreConcept]Blint the Underdelver^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BLINT_UNDERDELVER@NAME"
msgstr "Blint the Underdelver^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BLOOD_CLAN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Often looked down on by the other Giant Clans, the Blood Clan is a conglomeration of any breed of Demigiant imaginable. Loosely organized, the trolls and ogres of the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} indulge in their savage hierarchies—where for once no [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]actual Giant[/hyperlink] may boss them around."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BLOOD_CLAN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.BloodClanLoreConcept]Blood Clan[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@BLOOD_CLAN@TITLE"
msgstr "Blood Clan"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CAGE_OF_BINDING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "For a powerful {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, who can regularly escape death, there are few things more terrifying than a Cage of Binding. For such an enchanted shell, crafted from rare magic materials, represents the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and an eternity of nothingness. When sealed inside a Cage of Binding, a {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} will lose their arcane abilities and is rendered completely helpless. However, capturing a {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} inside is no small feat, and only few records in history speak of a wizard unfortunate enough to suffer such a gruesome fate."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CAGE_OF_BINDING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CageOfBindingLoreConcept]Cage of Binding[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CAGE_OF_BINDING@TITLE"
msgstr "Cage of Binding"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CALIOTH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CaliothLoreConcept]Calioth[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CALIOTH@NAME"
msgstr "Calioth^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CHAOS_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Chaos Affinity"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CINREN_TOLIATH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CinrenLoreConcept]Cinren Toliath^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CINREN_TOLIATH@NAME"
msgstr "Cinren Toliath^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CIRCLE_OF_DEOGAI@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "After the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TheFracturingLoreConcept]terrible disasters[/hyperlink] unleashed by the {GLOBAL.UnmakersLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} began to establish the Circles of Deogai throughout the cosmos. They were councils of {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} set on the most disputed worlds, each presided by an Archon arbiter. Through those Circles the Archons fostered stability and monitored the new magics devised by the <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> with a watchful eye.[br/][br/]By the time of the Fourth Age, most Circles of Deogai have either been destroyed or dispersed, and the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} turned to {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} as their primary forum of council. Yet some Circles are said to still persist, transformed by the ages until they were given new purpose."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CIRCLE_OF_DEOGAI@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept]Circle of Deogai[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@CIRCLE_OF_DEOGAI@TITLE"
msgstr "Circle of Deogai"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COLT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Renowned for their wealth, the Company of Lost Treasures is extending its influence across the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Specialized in hiring and outfitting skilled adventurers, the Company of Lost Treasures is uncovering and plundering the riches of ancient empires, above all from the ruined jewel of Giant kin, {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Often accused of shady practices, the officials of the Company have repeatedly proven that their contracts are always honored—one simply must pay attention to all the footnotes."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COLT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ColtLoreConcept]Company of Lost Treasures[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COLT@TITLE"
msgstr "Company of Lost Treasures"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COMMONWEALTH@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The empire of the Commonwealth was initially formed as a joining of races and cultures on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, aimed at the sharing of knowledge and the mutual protection of all. While these benign precepts held true for a time, ambition and technological advancement soon outgrew the concepts of the original charter, leading to much strife between factions within and without.[br/][br/]When the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldGateLoreConcept]World Gates[/hyperlink] on Athla were reopened the most important figureheads of the Commonwealth, including Edward Portsmith, were defeated or disappeared. In the chaos and under the pressure of returning [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept]Wizard Kings[/hyperlink], the powerful empire dismantled into factions they once sought to unite."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COMMONWEALTH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CommonwealthLoreConcept]Commonwealth[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COMMONWEALTHI@TITLE"
msgstr "Commonwealth"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COVENANT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Covenant are a faction within the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept]Pantheon of Godir[/hyperlink], who seek to uphold ancient agreements of peace and stability, as written by the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in ages past. Their lawful tendencies often put them in direct opposition to the {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COVENANT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept]Covenant[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@COVENANT@TITLE"
msgstr "Covenant"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DAFAEL_DEA@NAME"
msgstr "Dafal Dea^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DAFAL_DEA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DafalDeaLoreConcept]Dafal Dea^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DECIMUS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DecimusLoreConcept]Decimus the Unwavering^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DECIMUS@NAME"
msgstr "Decimus the Unwavering^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_OVERLORD@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Few dare speak of them, lest it invite infernal notice or provoke their wrath. The inscrutable masters of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicPrinceLoreConcept]Demonic Regency[/hyperlink], and of many [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept]Obbadothan horrors[/hyperlink] besides, Demon Overlords are counted among the mightiest of their kind. Some believe they are ancient fiends ascended through ages of carnage, while others claim they are primordial evils woven into the very fabric of creation.[br/][br/]Whatever their true nature, Demon Overlords are ever eager to bargain. To those deemed worthy, they offer power drawn from the depths of Obbadoth, binding supplicants through pacts both potent and perilous. In this way, they became the unseen architects behind countless infernal covenants that ripple across the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept]Astral Sea[/hyperlink]."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_OVERLORD@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]Demonic Overlord[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_OVERLORD@TITLE"
msgstr "Demon Overlord"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_PRINCE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept]Obbadothan Royalty[/hyperlink] are a loose and ever-shifting assembly bound by infernal pacts. Each member has bargained with a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicOverlordLoreConcept]Demon Overlord[/hyperlink], trading autonomy for power. As such, entry into the regency is largely open to anyone, or anything willing to make the trade.[br/][br/]Most infamous among them are the Demonic Princes, who, next to their own sinister ambitions, act as the chief commanders of their Overlord across all {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Though ever wary that failure—or maliciously twisted pact clause—might see them swiftly supplanted or dragged down screaming into damnation."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_PRINCE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DemonicPrinceLoreConcept]Demonic Prince[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DEMONIC_PRINCE@TITLE"
msgstr "Demonic Prince"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DRAGONS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Dragons are among the first creatures that the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} gifted with life. The first of these, known as the Elder Dragons, would utilize their vast intelligence and mastery of the elements to aid the Archons in shaping the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]Worlds[/hyperlink] within the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} as well as in crafting powerful artifacts. In all of this, they would be forced to work alongside the {GLOBAL.GiantsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, which led to much conflict.[br/][br/]Dragons come in three forms: firstly, the Elder Dragons who were born at the beginning of creation and on occasion ascend to [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept]Godirhood[/hyperlink] through their primal mastery of the arcane arts. Secondly, their offspring, the more common Dragons. Lastly, the far younger and less sophisticated Wyverns, who were hatched in ages since that primordial time. Beyond that, Dragons come in myriad types that are mostly associated with a different element, and some have even been raised as undead versions of their previous selves."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DRAGONS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Dragons[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DRAGONS@TITLE"
msgstr "Dragons"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DREAMERS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The origin and nature of the Dreamers is debated with controversy among {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Their protectors, the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, claim they are the children of the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and that they were sent to bring an end to [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath’s corruption[/hyperlink]. In the records of the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the Dreamers are attributed with immense creative powers, dreaming creatures, people, and entire worlds into existence. Such pure creation from nothingness is otherwise only observable with {GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, which indeed some beliefs identify as the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DREAMERS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DreamersLoreConcept]Dreamers[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DREAMERS@TITLE"
msgstr "The Dreamers"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Duatha, also known as the Fey Realm, is the home [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]world[/hyperlink] to some of the most notorious creatures. It is a place filled with deception and trickery, where nothing is as it seems and any expectations of common sense can be defied. Those who dare stray into Duatha’s mists are doomed to get lost in it forever—and said to be brought before the realm’s lords, the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, for judgment."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept]Duatha[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHA@TITLE"
msgstr "Duatha"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHADAE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Shrouds and mysteries surround the Duathadae, lords of the Fey realm {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. For all that is known, they are very protective of the lands under their undisputed rule, and their subjects, sometimes capricious, sometimes outright malicious, obey their word, be it through fear or adoration.[br/][br/]There is occasional evidence that their arcane powers may outmatch those of even a {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, but never have the Duathadae been known to leave their realm {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}; nor was a {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to this day foolish enough to challenge them in their own domain."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHADAE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept]Duathadae[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@DUATHADAE@TITLE"
msgstr "Duathadae"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@EDWARD@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EdwardLoreConcept]Edward Portsmith^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@EDWARD@NAME"
msgstr "Edward Portsmith^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDER_VAMPIRE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Elder Vampires are ageless undead blessed with nightborn powers, dominating the minds of their thralls and drinking the blood of their enemies. They must shun the sun, but thrive in their Sunless domains spreading from the shadows of their castles.[br/][br/]All Elder Vampires are connected through ancient blood lines, dating back to the <<m:{GLOBAL.ArchvampireLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> and the curse of the storied [hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrvatoghLoreConcept]Pale Prince[/hyperlink]. Due to this, a strong awareness of origin dictates the hierarchies among Vampires and their undead nobility. Still, even an Elder Vampire Hybrid may rise to fame after devouring the power of many Purebloods..."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDER_VAMPIRE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ElderVampireLoreConcept]Elder Vampire[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDER_VAMPIRE@TITLE"
msgstr "Elder Vampire"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGNS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Wizards banished to the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink} must endure the {GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Those that fail the trial lose themselves to madness and become [hyperlink,GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept]Lost Wizards[/hyperlink]. Some of these unfortunate souls, however, continue to grow their power until they regain a twisted fraction of sanity as Eldritch Sovereigns. Mangled, shattered, and deconstructed, their powers allow them to pierce the planar veils, unleashing their corrupting ambitions on the worlds. One of their most fearsome talents is their ability to enthrall not just creatures such as {GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, but even entire races to their will."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGNS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EldritchSovereignLoreConcept]Eldritch Sovereign[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELDRITCH_SOVEREIGNS@TITLE"
msgstr "Eldritch Sovereign"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELYA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Elya is a young {GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, a mystical species of benevolent [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept]Astral Sea Creatures[/hyperlink]. Unlike many others of her people, Elya feels a strong connection to mortals and the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Her youth and curiosity bring her closer to {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} - and danger - than any other of her kind would dare."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELYA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ElyaLoreConcept]Elya[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ELYA@TITLE"
msgstr "Elya"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENAMRU@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EnamruLoreConcept]Enam'ru Enkhanan^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENAMRU@NAME"
msgstr "Enam'ru Enkhanan^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Endailon are powerful cosmic entities from ancient times. They appear to be heavily linked to the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AffinitiesLoreConcept]Magic Affinities[/hyperlink], to the point that some {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} believe that the magic of the cosmos is a manifestation of the Endailon rather than the Endailon being mere manifestations of the affinities themselves.[br/][br/]Emerging myths surround the Endailon, depicting them as the original gods alongside the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who shaped the cosmos and ruled the races throughout. But there is little evidence of the Endailon's motivations and whether or not they concern themselves with the affairs of mortals. In ages past, the Endailon [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept]clashed with the Archons[/hyperlink], leading to their imprisonment within {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Now, with the opening of {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, they roam freely again and will leave their mark on the cosmos once more."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept]Endailon[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON@TITLE"
msgstr "Endailon"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON_CRISIS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Little is known about the Endailon Crisis, though it has become a topic of great interest among the scholars of {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. What has been established as commonly accepted knowledge, is that the Endailon Crisis happened in a distant age, before the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TurielLoreConcept]first Godir[/hyperlink] set foot on {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. It was a conflict of cosmic scale, involving the {GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and possibly factions under their influence on one side, and the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their allies—notably among them the {GLOBAL.AncientKrazuraLoreConcept.Hyperlink}—on the other. The Endailon Crisis ended with the {GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} becoming locked within {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON_CRISIS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept]Endailon Crisis[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ENDAILON_CRISIS@TITLE"
msgstr "Endailon Crisis"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_COUNCIL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Originally, the Eternal Council was founded as a council of <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>, where the matters of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the many {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} which it spanned would be discussed under the honorary leadership of the Titans. Later, when the {GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} had revoked any allegiance to the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, only the wisest of the Giant Kings remained in the Eternal Council. They moved the seat of the council away from Titan’s Henge and indeed their discussions focused less and less on the government of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, but instead on the mysteries of the cosmos.[br/][br/]In scholarly union, the Eternal Council explored the various applications of crystal magic, seeking to employ Lithorite to immortalize their knowledge—and at last themselves. As their opus magnum, the Eternal Council transferred their souls into Lithorite crystals, escaping Archon judgment and becoming the {GLOBAL.EternalSagesLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_COUNCIL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EternalCouncilLoreConcept]Eternal Council[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_COUNCIL@TITLE"
msgstr "Eternal Council"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_SAGES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Once the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EternalCouncilLoreConcept]wisest Giant Kings[/hyperlink] of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the Eternal Sages have left behind their mortal bodies, transferring their souls into Lithorite crystals. They are wielders of powerful crystal magic, commanding the Lithorine and blessing their followers with large stature and crystalline resilience.[br/][br/]The Eternal Sages no longer concern themselves much with the matters of mortals. Instead, all their actions are directed towards the collection and preservation of knowledge, which they store in vast crystal libraries of their own making. It is said that the Eternal Sages know the answer to every enigma the cosmos holds, yet persuading them to share any such knowledge can be a task for eternity."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_SAGES@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.EternalSagesLoreConcept]Eternal Sages[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ETERNAL_SAGES@TITLE"
msgstr "Eternal Sages"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FANGIR@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FangirLoreConcept]Fangir^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FANGIR@NAME"
msgstr "{LOC.LORDS@HERO_FIRSTNAME_17@NAME} {LOC.LORDS@HERO_SECONDNAME_17@NAME}"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FAUSTER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FausterTheMeticulousLoreConcept]Fauster the Meticulous^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FAUSTER_METICULOUS@NAME"
msgstr "Fauster the Meticulous^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FFLAMMYCH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AyaLoreConcept]Fflammych Fyre-Heart^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FFLAMMYCH@NAME"
msgstr "Fflammych Fyre-Heart^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FIRE_CLAN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The most aggressive of the Giant Clans, the Fire Clan often seeks direct confrontation with the Rulers of a realm. Claiming distant heritage of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, these Giants like to unleash terrible war beasts and wage war on the people settling in the lands they regard as their own."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FIRE_CLAN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FireClanLoreConcept]Fire Clan[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FIRE_CLAN@TITLE"
msgstr "Fire Clan"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FJALLA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AyaLoreConcept]Fjalla Tor-Builder^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FJALLA@NAME"
msgstr "Fjalla Tor-Builder^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FRACTURE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Fractures are tears in the very fabric of magic, altering any spell cast near them. They were the byproduct of the {GLOBAL.UnmakersLoreConcept.Hyperlink}' experiments and often appear around their ruins and magical wastes. Exposure to these fractures, or to the inward winds they produce, can mutate both mana and life itself.[br/][br/]Fractures grow unstable and increase in size as they swallow and twist magic, to a point where they can explode; scattering Astral Barrens, contaminating the area, and creating new fractures. A great number of unstable Fractures in a realm can cause a massive calamity, such as the cataclysm known as {GLOBAL.TheFracturingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FRACTURE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FractureLoreConcept]Fracture[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FRACTURE@TITLE"
msgstr "Fracture"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FREDRIC@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FredricLoreConcept]Fredric the Twice-Cursed[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FREDRIC@NAME"
msgstr "Fredric the Twice-Cursed^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FRIKKA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.FrikkaLoreConcept]Frikka Dynosis^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FRIKKA@NAME"
msgstr "Frikka Dynosis^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@FROST_CLAN@NAME"
msgstr "Frost Clan"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GEASSADAE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "As the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their Mistwalker servants became a greater threat to the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the general interest in the Fey realm {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} was rekindled, since old lore might expose the Duathadae's unknown weaknesses. The search through ancient scriptures and chronicles revealed that once a {GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept.Hyperlink} had existed on {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, and—more importantly—that the {GLOBAL.DuathadaeLoreConcept.Hyperlink} may not be the only lords of the Fey.[br/][br/]Myths about the Geassadae were uncovered, powerful Fey who may have once ruled {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, before falling victim to the Duathadae's dark enchantments. Though it has been warned that such tales may only be a perfidious variant of Fey trickery themselves."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GEASSADAE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GeassadaeLoreConcept]Geassadae[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GEASSADAE@TITLE"
msgstr "Geassadae"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A relatively rare but imposing sight to behold, giants once roamed the primordial {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in greater numbers. In the early days of the cosmos, giants directed the flow of the land and shaped the continents upon each world. This purportedly piqued the ire of the {GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who had formed worlds in a certain way before the giants and were unimpressed with their later adjustments.[br/][br/]True giants tend to come in various forms, usually associated with an element that they have a certain amount of control over. A number of offshoot races of Giantkin and other subtypes have also come into being over the ages through various intermingling of races."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANTS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantsLoreConcept]Giants[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANTS@TITLE"
msgstr "Giants"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANT_KING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Sometimes Elder Giants, sometimes Giants of younger ages blessed with immense power and size, the Giant Kings trace their regal claim on the realms back to the Giant kingdom of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Masters of the forge and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]shapers of worlds[/hyperlink], the Giant Kings are primal forces to be reckoned with. Gladly they will tell tales about the days of the Great Hunt, when Elder Giants tamed the {GLOBAL.UrwildernessLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and slew its Primordial Beasts."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANT_KING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept]Giant King[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GIANT_KING@TITLE"
msgstr "Giant King"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GLOOMWATCH@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Gloomwatch is a diverse faction, incorporating many different races and cultures. They are united by their worship of the {GLOBAL.AffinitiesLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the {GLOBAL.DreamersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their eternal fight against the forces of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Their alleged history dates back to the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their first leader Irith of the Scrying Fountain, chronicling a mythic tale of how the {GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the {GLOBAL.SyronLoreConcept.Hyperlink} descended from these celestial origins."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GLOOMWATCH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept]Gloomwatch[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GLOOMWATCH@TITLE"
msgstr "Gloomwatch"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GLOOM_HOOKNAIL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GloomHooknailLoreConcept]Gloom Hooknail^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GLOOM_HOOKNAIL@NAME"
msgstr "Gloom Hooknail^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GODIR@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Wizards of the {GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who gather at {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are called Godir. From there they seek new knowledge and journey to new realms in the Astral Sea. Some of the Godir are newly <<m:{GLOBAL.AscendedChampLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>—while others are ancient <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> or [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Elder Dragons[/hyperlink], seeking dominion over new realms and people through their mastery of the {GLOBAL.AffinitiesLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Godir have achieved a form of immortality: if they are vanquished, they are cast into the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and seek to rematerialize in Magehaven."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GODIR@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept]Godir[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GODIR@TITLE"
msgstr "Godir"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREAT_UMBRAL_WAR@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Great Umbral War broke out when {GLOBAL.LithylLoreConcept.Hyperlink} launched an invasion on {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, unleashing the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept]swarming hordes[/hyperlink] of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink} from the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Yet it was only the beginning, for soon thereafter <<m:{GLOBAL.EldritchSovereignLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> all across the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} began similar assaults, enshrouding the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} with their corruptive gloom.[br/][br/]Though the {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} attained the aid of the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and later the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the enemy is tenacious and its maddening reach can corrupt even Godir. Therefore much hope is placed in the powers of the {GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, despite their unfathomable influence and motives."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREAT_UMBRAL_WAR@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GreatUmbralWarLoreConcept]Great Umbral War[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREAT_UMBRAL_WAR@TITLE"
msgstr "Great Umbral War"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREXOLIS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A fractured [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]World[/hyperlink] hidden in the mists of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. The {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} left a custodian to guard the secrets which lie buried here."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREXOLIS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept]Grexolis[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@GREXOLIS@TITLE"
msgstr "Grexolis"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HAM_BINGER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HamBingerLoreConcept]Ham Binger^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HAM_BINGER@NAME"
msgstr "Ham Binger^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HORWYND@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When the {GLOBAL.AncientKrazuraLoreConcept.Hyperlink} became locked in {GLOBAL.GrexolisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, their distant relatives, the Horwynd, took it upon themselves to preserve their knowledge and memory. They fled from the sphere of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink] influence and no chronicles speak of their destination or fate.[br/][br/]And yet they returned ages later, revealing the Shrouded Isles they created through unbreakable pacts with the <<m:{GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>. With pride they eulogize their Tree of Wisdom and its schools of magic. But their homeland and its history remain a mortal secret."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HORWYND@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept]Horwynd[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HORWYND@TITLE"
msgstr "Horwynd"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HRIMIS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HrimisLoreConcept]Hrímis Glacier-Carver[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HRIMIS@NAME"
msgstr "Hrímis Glacier-Carver^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HYKA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.HykaLoreConcept]Hyka-Tha Agatare[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@HYKA@NAME"
msgstr "Hyka-Tha Agatare^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@INSECTOIDWARDEN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.InsectoidWardenLoreConcept]Ryc'turi^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@INSECTOIDWARDEN@NAME"
msgstr "Ryc'turi^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@JULIA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.JuliaLoreConcept]Julia of House Inioch[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@JULIA@NAME"
msgstr "Julia of House Inioch^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KARISSA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.KarissaLoreConcept]Karissa the Red^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KARISSA@NAME"
msgstr "Karissa the Red^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KHIR_URANON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.KhirUranonLoreConcept]Khir Uranon^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KHIR_URANON@NAME"
msgstr "Khir Uranon^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KLEDAS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.KledasLoreConcept]Kledas the Artist[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KLEDAS@NAME"
msgstr "Kledas the Artist^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KRUUL_BLIGHTLORD@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.KruulBlightlordLoreConcept]Kruul Blightlord^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@KRUUL_BLIGHTLORD@NAME"
msgstr "Kruul Blightlord^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LARYSSA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LaryssaLoreConcept]Laryssa Mirabilis^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LARYSSA@NAME"
msgstr "Laryssa Mirabilis^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LITHYL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LithylLoreConcept]Lithyl Nightweaver^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LITHYL@NAME"
msgstr "Lithyl Nightweaver^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LITHYL_TRUE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LithylTrueLoreConcept]Lithyl Nightweaver^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LITHYL_TRUE@NAME"
msgstr "Lithyl Nightweaver^F (True Form)"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LORDS@BHAJIF_RACE@BIO"
msgstr "Be there an ancient artifact to uncover or a cosmic event to unfold, the Wanderer is ever present. Many question whether he follows the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept]Astral Flows[/hyperlink] to fortune, or whether fortune follows him instead. Is he the moth or the flame?[br/][br/]Bhajif refers to those who follow him as the Lost Travelers, for they walk in the footsteps of a man without direction. When his followers ask Bhajif what path they should take, he always replies: \"Travelers, there is no path, for the path is made through walking.\""

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LOST_MAGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A Lost Wizard was once a powerful wizard who, either by foolhardy choice or forced exile, found themselves in the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and succumbed to the {GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. These power-hungry husks now glide with deadly purpose through the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} as one of the myriad [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept]Monsters[/hyperlink] that roam its depths, preying upon the unwary.[br/][br/]While it retains an affinity for magic and even clutches its [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TomeLoreConcept]Tome of Spells[/hyperlink] greedily, its physical form has twisted to match its [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept]environment[/hyperlink]."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LOST_MAGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept]Lost Wizard[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@LOST_MAGE@TITLE"
msgstr "Lost Wizard"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAER@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Maer are a rare breed of sentient merfolk, residing deep within the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Where mortals find travel through the Astral Sea tedious and dangerous, these beings move through it with ease and grace, singing along to songs no one else can hear.[br/][br/]The Maer are such a rare sight that many schooled mortals deem their existence a myth, a story of solace to explain the strange sounds heard during the travels through the Astral Sea. But these benevolent, solitary creatures of magic and song are as real as the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept]horrors[/hyperlink] that plague the currents."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAER@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept]Maer[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAER@TITLE"
msgstr "Maer"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGEHAVEN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Magehaven is a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]World[/hyperlink] in the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} where the {GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} hold their most important forum of dispute and council. It is protected by an unbreakable spell which prevents any harm from being done to a living creature or [hyperlink,GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept]Soul[/hyperlink]. Therefore, even the fiercest enemies can meet there to negotiate their conflicts.[br/][br/]Magehaven is located close to {GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and bears remnants of the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who once dwelt there. Among the many wonders of Magehaven are the Library of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TomeLoreConcept]Ancient Tomes[/hyperlink] and the {GLOBAL.WorldGateLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, which act as magic portals through the Astral Sea."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGEHAVEN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept]Magehaven[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGEHAVEN@TITLE"
msgstr "Magehaven"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGELOCKS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Magelock weapons are magic-powered ranged weapons, derived from the ordnance created by mighty empires long since fallen. By fusing the arcane with the physical, Magelock mechanisms allow skilled marksmen to hit faraway targets with great impact and accuracy.[br/][br/]Magelock weaponry permeates all corners of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, implying analogous origins on various realms, yet the remnants of the ruined {GLOBAL.CommonwealthLoreConcept.Hyperlink} remain most infamous for wielding these terrible weapons."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGELOCKS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MagelocksLoreConcept]Magelock[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MAGELOCKS@TITLE"
msgstr "Magelock Weaponry"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MALIEL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MalielLoreConcept]Maliel[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MALIEL@NAME"
msgstr "Maliel^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MATERIUM_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Materium"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MEANDOR@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MeandorLoreConcept]Meandor^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MEGAIRA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MegairaLoreConcept]Megaira the Scalded^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MEGAIRA@NAME"
msgstr "Megaira the Scalded^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MELENIS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MelenisLoreConcept]Melenis^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MERLIN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MerlinLoreConcept]Merlin^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MERLIN@NAME"
msgstr "Merlin^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MESHARA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MesharaLoreConcept]Meshara the Radiant^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MESHARA@NAME"
msgstr "Meshara the Radiant^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MORTAL_RACES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "WIP Mortal Races Tooltip"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MORTAL_RACES@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MortalRacesLoreConcept]Mortal Races[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MORTAL_RACES@TITLE"
msgstr "Mortal Races"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MYRRIDA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Many myths surround the fabled kingdom of Myrrida, where <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> once ruled the small races across the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Undeniable is the wealth and grandeur, still exhibited within its ruined monumental structures and cities. Yet there is much debate among {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} about the fall of Myrrida. Some say the <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> became corrupted by their power, giving rise to the {GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Others blame [hyperlink,GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept]Archon[/hyperlink] suppression for the destruction of a lost utopia.[br/][br/]Certain is that the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and their allied [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Elder Dragons[/hyperlink] besieged Myrrida, ending the long Age of Giants and distantly presaging the {GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. While the various Giant Clans seek to carry on the legacy of their ancient forefathers, their deeds pale beside the marveled legends of Myrrida."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MYRRIDA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept]Myrrida[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@MYRRIDA@TITLE"
msgstr "Myrrida^N"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NATURE_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Nature Affinity"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NEKRON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NekronLoreConcept]Nekron the Risen^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NEKRON@NAME"
msgstr "Nekron the Risen^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NIMUE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NimueLoreConcept]Nimue^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NOCTUS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.NoctusLoreConcept]Noctus^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@NOCTUS@NAME"
msgstr "Noctus^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@OBBADOTH@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Obbadoth is an infernal [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]World[/hyperlink] ruled by Demonic Princes, where fiends make the laws and sins are virtuous. Many realms of this world are affected by spells which enhance one's primal urges, which often leads to bloodshed, debauchery, and everything in between. Very few {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} can withstand Obbadoth's infernal influence."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@OBBADOTH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ObbadothLoreConcept]Obbadoth[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@OBBADOTH@TITLE"
msgstr "Obbadoth"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ONERON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.OneronLoreConcept]O'neron^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ONERON@NAME"
msgstr "O'neron^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ORDER_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Order Affinity"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@OTTO_THE_DISCARDED@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.OttoDiscardedLoreConcept]Otto the Discarded^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@OTTO_THE_DISCARDED@NAME"
msgstr "Otto the Discarded^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PANTHEON@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "With many [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept]Wizard Kings[/hyperlink] seeing themselves as living gods, it is no surprise their gathering at {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink} became known as the Pantheon. In this sanctuary the members of the Pantheon debate and scheme to alter the fate of the cosmos. The Pantheon consists of many factions and alliances, of which the {GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and {GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are most prominent."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PANTHEON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept]Pantheon[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PANTHEON@TITLE"
msgstr "Pantheon"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PELLARI@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Not much is known about the Pellari, for reports from the Fey realm {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} are scarce and notoriously unreliable. What has been accepted as common knowledge is that the Pellari are a diverse group of different animalistic races which are united by their display of almost excessive friendliness and a preference for simple, pastoral life.[br/][br/]Some sources pick up on the theory that {GLOBAL.DuathaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is a [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DreamersLoreConcept]Dreamer[/hyperlink] and propose that the Pellari are one of her childish creations; a proposition that often gets extended to the Fey themselves and their unique magic properties that seem to defy all arcane rules and reason."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PELLARI@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.PellariLoreConcept]Pellari[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PELLARI@TITLE"
msgstr "Pellari"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PETRAS_CELENA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.PetrasCelenaLoreConcept]Petras Celena[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PETRAS_CELENA@NAME"
msgstr "Petras Celena^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PRIMALSPIRITS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Primal Spirits are spiritual representations of the many aspects of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.NatureConcept]Nature[/hyperlink], worshiped by various peoples in the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Each Spirit brings its own doctrines on society, and followers look up to them for guidance throughout all aspects of life. There are many different beliefs surrounding these spirits, but they all have one thing in common: in battle their worshipers can call upon the powers of their chosen Spirit to empower and aid them. The most common Primal Spirits are the Sylvan Wolf, Ash Sabertooth, Mire Crocodile, Dune Serpent, Storm Crow, Glacial Mammoth, and Tunneling Spider."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PRIMALSPIRITS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.PrimalSpiritsLoreConcept]Primal Spirits[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@PRIMALSPIRITS@TITLE"
msgstr "Primal Spirits"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@RACHEQ@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RacheqLoreConcept]Ra'cheq the Disturbing^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@RACHEQ@NAME"
msgstr "Ra'cheq the Disturbing^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@RAINA_THE_GOLDEN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RainaTheGoldenLoreConcept]Raina the Golden^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@RAINA_THE_GOLDEN@NAME"
msgstr "Raina the Golden^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@REVENANTS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Once {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} in life, the soul-cursed Revenants invoke the greatest fear in the enemies of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. For their unlife represents the ultimate triumph of corruption, when not even the most virtuous souls may escape. First encountered on [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]Worlds[/hyperlink] locked through [hyperlink,GLOBAL.SealLoreConcept]Seals[/hyperlink], the Revenant curse has since then spread to many Necropolises which the Archons left behind in their cosmic wars."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@REVENANTS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RevenantsLoreConcept]Revenants[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@REVENANTS@TITLE"
msgstr "Revenants"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@ROOT_NODE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.RootNodeLoreConcept]Root Node[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_ARTIFICING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The disciples of the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink} School of Artificing diligently collect and preserve magical artifacts and monuments. When the Scholars of Shrouding proposed to cache the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept]Godir's[/hyperlink] secrets in the <<m:{GLOBAL.ShroudedIsleConcept.Hyperlink}>>, the Scholars of Artificing drew on their expertise in magical structures to construct the Portals that connect these hidden Realms to the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_ARTIFICING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SchoolOfArtificingLoreConcept]School of Artificing[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_ARTIFICING@TITLE"
msgstr "School of Artificing"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_SHROUDING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The disciples of the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink} School of Shrouding were conservators and archivists of secret knowledge found in the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. When the development of experimental spells was repressed by the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the guileful Scholars of Shrouding suggested securing them in the <<m:{GLOBAL.ShroudedIsleConcept.Hyperlink}>>, while also shrouding the Portals that lead to them."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_SHROUDING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SchoolOfShroudingLoreConcept]School of Shrouding[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_SHROUDING@TITLE"
msgstr "School of Shrouding"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_VITALIZING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The disciples of the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink} School of Vitalizing were primarily conservators and breeders of flora and fauna. Once the <<m:{GLOBAL.ShroudedIsleConcept.Hyperlink}>> were shaped, the Scholars of Vitalizing applied their knowledge of growth and life to create regenerating habitats, where the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept]Godir's[/hyperlink] sanctuaries remain untouched by the oppression of the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_VITALIZING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SchoolOfVitalizingLoreConcept]School of Vitalizing[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_VITALIZING@TITLE"
msgstr "School of Vitalizing"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_WARDING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The disciples of the {GLOBAL.HorwyndLoreConcept.Hyperlink} School of Warding were originally tasked with preserving knowledge of battle and war. When the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} established the <<m:{GLOBAL.CircleOfDeogaiLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>, the School of honorable warriors and knights deployed their holy power to protect the Portals to the <<m:{GLOBAL.ShroudedIsleConcept.Hyperlink}>> against invading forces and the inquisitive agents of the Archons."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_WARDING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SchoolOfWardingLoreConcept]School of Warding[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SCHOOL_OF_WARDING@TITLE"
msgstr "School of Warding"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SERENA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SerenaLoreConcept]Serena^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_AFFINITY@TITLE"
msgstr "Shadow Affinity"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_DEMONS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Umbral Demons, sometimes referred to as Shadow Demons, are molded by {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Their forbidden inception reputedly involves distorting corrupted souls into the shapes of the Umbral Demons. The tainted creatures feed on magic leaking from the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They first consumed the world of their creation, until only the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink} remained: A twisted husk filled with blackness and despair. Since then, the Umbral Demons have preyed on many worlds, including {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, allowing the Umbral Abyss to spread in their wake."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_DEMONS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept]Umbral Demons[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_DEMONS@TITLE"
msgstr "Umbral Demons"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_REALM@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Beyond the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and even the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept]Void[/hyperlink] an eldritch infestation lurks: The Umbral Abyss, the dominion of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Here is where {GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} reign, molded through a vile corruption of the power of Creation itself. Vile and toxic to any living being, the Umbral Abyss ever seeks to corrupt the Astral Sea, tearing festering wounds into the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. The {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink} fight back against the corruption, but wherever they wage war, the scars of battle that stain the realms never fully heal.[br/][br/]Through the Ages, the Umbral Abyss has claimed many civilizations, and their remnants of knowledge and treasure have lured many adventurers and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WizardKingLoreConcept]wizards[/hyperlink] to a fate many consider worse than death."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_REALM@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept]Umbral Abyss[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_REALM@TITLE"
msgstr "Umbral Abyss"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_TRIAL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In the darkness of the {GLOBAL.AstralVoidLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the banished Wizards are tormented by visions and maddening voices. Survivors describe vastly different experiences, as if the cosmos creates a reckoning for a Wizard's individual actions and beliefs. Those that succumb are doomed to drift forever as a <<m:{GLOBAL.LostWizardLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>>, mad husks of which little remains other than their lust for power."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_TRIAL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadowTrialLoreConcept]Torment of Shadows[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADOW_TRIAL@TITLE"
msgstr "Torment of Shadows"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADRAI@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "A group of ambitious {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who formed a volatile cabal in order to claim power within the {GLOBAL.PantheonLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They believe no power should be hidden from anyone and are known for their schemes and invasions of realms they deem worthy of their domination. Their chaotic tendencies often put them in direct opposition to the {GLOBAL.CovenantFactionLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. "

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADRAI@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShadraiFactionLoreConcept]Shad'rai[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHADRAI@TITLE"
msgstr "Shad'rai"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHIRA@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ShiraLoreConcept]Shira Snowblood^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SHIRA@NAME"
msgstr "Shira Snowblood^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SINGAITH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.AyaLoreConcept]Singaith Sky-Shatter^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SINGAITH@NAME"
msgstr "Singaith Sky-Shatter^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SKONYRU@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SkonyruLoreConcept]Skonyru^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SKONYRU@NAME"
msgstr "Skonyru^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SOULS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Souls are the eternal Astral manifestations of all living beings. When someone dies, their soul is released to return to [hyperlink,GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept]the Well of Creation[/hyperlink]. This journey through the {GLOBAL.AstralFlowsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} is arduous and many {GLOBAL.AstralDwellersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} hunt these souls. Especially troubled souls may find themselves lost or captured during the journey.[br/][br/]With specific magics, souls can be captured for nefarious purposes. Some dark races use souls as a valuable currency that allows the summoning of undead beings."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SOULS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept]Souls[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SOULS@TITLE"
msgstr "Souls"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STONE_CLAN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Persistent and steady as stone, the Rock Clan has the patience to build what the other Giant Clans can only dream of conquering. They shun contact with the smaller races, going to great lengths to keep their dungeon halls, where faint echoes of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept]Myrrida’s splendor[/hyperlink] are recalled, inaccessible."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STONE_CLAN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.StoneClanLoreConcept]Rock Clan[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STONE_CLAN@TITLE"
msgstr "Rock Clan"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STORM_CLAN@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "First silent then tempestuous, the Storm Clan prefers to strike when it is the least expected. The leaders of this Giant Clan study the lost magic of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, seeking to emulate the arcane powers of the <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> of old."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STORM_CLAN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.StormClanLoreConcept]Storm Clan[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@STORM_CLAN@TITLE"
msgstr "Storm Clan"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SUNDREN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SundrenLoreConcept]Sundren^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYLVANI_LAUREL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SylvaniLaurelLoreConcept]Sylvani Laurel^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYLVANI_LAUREL@NAME"
msgstr "Sylvani Laurel^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYRON@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Originally descendants of the {GLOBAL.MaerLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the first Syrons were a part of the {GLOBAL.GloomwatchLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to protect the {GLOBAL.DreamersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} from the corrupting influence of {GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. They settled on idyllic worlds where the light of the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink}’s creation still burned bright, until the {GLOBAL.ShadowDemonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} eventually invaded. Most of the Syrons were massacred and many of the survivors enslaved, their devoured home worlds overrun by the {GLOBAL.ShadowRealmLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. The few Syrons that escaped spread across the Astral Sea, but many found themselves locked in an endless crusade against the Umbral Demons, even if they formally abandoned the Gloomwatch long ago."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYRON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SyronLoreConcept]Syrons[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYRON@TITLE"
msgstr "Syrons"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYRON_SOVEREIGN@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SyronSovereignLoreConcept]Nykareth^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@SYRON_SOVEREIGN@NAME"
msgstr "Nykareth^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TEPHRADENIR@NAME"
msgstr "{LOC.LORDS@HERO_FIRSTNAME_1@NAME}"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_FRACTURING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Fracturing was the magical cataclysm that erased the {GLOBAL.UnmakersLoreConcept.Hyperlink} from the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and brought an end to their experiments. The few stories that survived the calamity speak of [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FractureLoreConcept]Fractures[/hyperlink] suddenly growing and erupting in a chain reaction.[br/][br/]Through the Fracturing, the affected worlds were changed forever. The land became barren, magic turned hazardous; some of their inhabitants adapted, and some were altered beyond recognition."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_FRACTURING@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TheFracturingLoreConcept]the Fracturing[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_FRACTURING@TITLE"
msgstr "The Fracturing"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_WELL@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "According to mythology, the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} pulled the cosmos from the Well of Creation. All later creations of the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink} would date back to this one wonder. From {GLOBAL.MagehavenLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, located deep in the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the Well can be seen as a looming bright omen, a slowly swirling white maelstrom from which the light of creation emerges in shifting directions. All <<c:{GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> of the dead are drawn to return to the Well on their final journey."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_WELL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TheWellLoreConcept]the Well[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@THE_WELL@TITLE"
msgstr "The Well"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TIDOLON@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Tidolon is known for its vast oceans and relatively low density of land. Islands and small continents dot the massive sea of blue. Many aquatic beings thrive on this [hyperlink,GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept]World[/hyperlink], and it is said many lost treasures and whole empires are hidden beneath its surface."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TIDOLON@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TidolonLoreConcept]Tidolon[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TIDOLON@TITLE"
msgstr "Tidolon"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TOMES@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Tomes of power hold certain fundamental truths and secrets of the cosmos, often associated with specific {GLOBAL.AffinitiesLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. These works are mystical manuscripts written by beings of power like {GLOBAL.GodirLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, to pass on their mastery of the subject within.[br/][br/]True mastery of a Tome can only be achieved through dedicated focus. Every stage of mastery will grant powers that can alter realms and even a Godir's subjects themselves."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TOMES@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TomeLoreConcept]Tome[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TOMES@TITLE"
msgstr "Tomes of Knowledge"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KINGCULT@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TraitorKingCultLoreConcept]Sons of the Kjörnoe[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KINGS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Traitor Kings were the <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> of old {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} who broke allegiance to the Titans, ending the ancient agreement between Elder Giants and {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Drunk on the glory of their kingdom they rejected a faith centered on the {GLOBAL.AllfatherLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, proclaiming that the <<m:{GLOBAL.GiantKingLoreConcept.Hyperlink}>> themselves had acted as gods and should therefore be worshiped as such.[br/][br/]Acting as ruthless overlords the Traitor Kings engaged in dark magic, twisting stolen knowledge from the {GLOBAL.EternalCouncilLoreConcept.Hyperlink} to achieve immortality. Yet when the war with the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Elder Dragons[/hyperlink] reached their thrones, they fell one by one, leaving only myths of their corrupt souls still haunting the ruins of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KINGS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept]Traitor Kings[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KINGS@TITLE"
msgstr "Traitor Kings"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KING_CULT@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Tempted by the promise of dark power, the Sons of the Kjörnoe worship the fallen {GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink} as gods. Searching for artifacts imbued with the {GLOBAL.SoulsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} of their deceased masters, the Sons of the Kjörnoe study the forbidden soulcurses of the {GLOBAL.TraitorKingsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, claiming the lives of the innocent to empower their vile rituals."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TRAITOR_KING_CULT@TITLE"
msgstr "Sons of the Kjörnoe"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TUGRUM@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TugrumLoreConcept]Tugrum Hammerhall^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TUGRUM@NAME"
msgstr "Tugrum Hammerhall^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TURIEL@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.TurielLoreConcept]Turiel Tolarim^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@TURIEL@NAME"
msgstr "Turiel Tolarim^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@UNMAKERS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Unmakers were a group of ambitious wizards whose experiments devastated large sections of the {GLOBAL.AstralSeaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, now known as the Fractured Realms. They rose to power after the {GLOBAL.EndailonCrisisLoreConcept.Hyperlink} had destroyed or weakened the dominant forces of previous ages. Believing themselves capable of unraveling the very essence of mana and magic, the Unmakers competed and cooperated among themselves, striving to recreate the powers flowing from the Well of Creation.[br/][br/]Among the nomadic tribes of the Fractured Worlds, countless cautionary tales speak of the Unmakers and their experiments: how they tore the fabrics of magic, scarred the realms with [hyperlink,GLOBAL.FractureLoreConcept]Fractures[/hyperlink] — and ultimately, as the moral of the story, perished in the {GLOBAL.TheFracturingLoreConcept.Hyperlink} that reshaped the realms."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@UNMAKERS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.UnmakersLoreConcept]Unmakers[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@UNMAKERS@TITLE"
msgstr "Unmakers"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URRATH@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Urrath is the nemesis of the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink} and widely believed to be the bringer of darkness and corruption to the cosmos. The most terrifying creatures known to exist, such as the {GLOBAL.AstralMonstersLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, are blamed on Urrath's influence, as is all evil running through the veins of mortal races."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URRATH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrrathLoreConcept]Urrath[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URRATH@TITLE"
msgstr "Urrath"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URVATOGH@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrvatoghLoreConcept]Urvatogh[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URVATOGH@NAME"
msgstr "Urvatogh^M"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URWILDERNESS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "When the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.DragonsLoreConcept]Elder Dragons[/hyperlink] shaped the {GLOBAL.WorldsWithinLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, they aroused the great beasts dwelling in its raw primal shell. Calling upon the powers of the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.EndailonLoreConcept]Nature Endailon[/hyperlink], these Primordial Beasts surrounded themselves in an overgrown Urwilderness, where creatures of many vicious, but also graceful, designs came to be and that even the Elder Dragons and Giants shunned.[br/][br/]Thus, when the small races arrived on the realms, their spreading settlements soon clashed with the enduring jungle of the Urwilderness. Enraged by the intrusions of civilization, the Primordial Beasts started to rampage across the realms, destroying everything in their wake.[br/][br/]Moved by the woes of the small races, the [hyperlink,GLOBAL.GiantsLoreConcept]Elder Giants[/hyperlink] rose to their defense, initiating the Great Hunt. Gifted with the celestial chains of the {GLOBAL.ArchonsLoreConcept.Hyperlink}, the Elder Giants thinned out the Urwilderness and bound the Primordial Beasts within mighty prisons. It was the dawn of the Age of Giants and thereupon the founding of {GLOBAL.MyrridaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URWILDERNESS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.UrwildernessLoreConcept]Urwilderness[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@URWILDERNESS@TITLE"
msgstr "Urwilderness"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VALERY@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ValeryLoreConcept]Valery of House Avernos^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VALERY@NAME"
msgstr "Valery of House Avernos^F"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VALLEY_WONDERS@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "The Valley of Wonders is a historic area on the Blessed Continent on the world of {GLOBAL.AthlaLoreConcept.Hyperlink}. Once the home of the Elven Court of House Inioch, it has seen much turmoil since the first Athlan humans sacked the fabled court. It remains an area of great natural beauty and magical potency."

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VALLEY_WONDERS@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.ValleyofWondersLoreConcept]Valley of Wonders[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VALLEY_WONDERS@TITLE"
msgstr "Valley of Wonders"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VAULTSPHERE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.VaultsphereLoreConcept]Vaultsphere[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@VAULTSPHERE@TITLE"
msgstr "Vaultsphere"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@WEPWATEP@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.WepwatepLoreConcept]Wepwatep^F[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@WERLAC@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.WerlacLoreConcept]Werlac of Insaldur^M[/hyperlink]"

msgid "INTERFACE@LORE_CONCEPT@WERLAC@NAME"
msgstr "Werlac of Insaldur^M"

