msgid "INTERFACE@TEXT@LAVA@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Lava is a type of terrain that can appear both on the surface and underground. When a {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} annexes a {GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink} with lava, they suffer a {GLOBAL.CityStabilityConcept.Hyperlink} penalty. This penalty can be avoided by having either the Underground or Desolate Adaptation.[br/][br/]If the center of a province is in lava, then you will be able to build a {GLOBAL.MineConcept.Hyperlink} or {GLOBAL.ConduitConcept.Hyperlink} {GLOBAL.ProvinceImprovementConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/]Units that can traverse lava need to have one of the following:[bulletlist][bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.FLYING_MOVEMENT.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.FLOATING_MOVEMENT.Hyperlink}[bullet/]{GLOBAL.PROPERTIES.LAVA_WALK.Hyperlink}[/bulletlist]"

