msgid "INTERFACE@TEXT@SIEGE@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "If a {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} has a {GLOBAL.CityWallStructureConcept.Hyperlink} and you wish to conquer it, you first need to besiege it and breach its defenses.[br/][br/]A Siege can be initiated by attacking any of the 7 {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} hexes with at least 1 {GLOBAL.ArmyConcept.Hyperlink} led by a {GLOBAL.HeroConcept.Hyperlink} which must remain adjacent to the city until the siege is completed or else the Siege is lifted.[br/][br/]While sieging the City's {GLOBAL.FortificationHealthConcept.Hyperlink} is lowered by the besieger's {GLOBAL.FortificationDamageConcept.Hyperlink}.[br/][br/] <<m:{GLOBAL.SiegeProjectConcept.Hyperlink}>> can be used to speed up the siege by dealing more {GLOBAL.FortificationDamageConcept.Hyperlink}. They can also remove defenses and give the besieger an advantage.[br/][br/]Once {GLOBAL.FortificationHealthConcept.Hyperlink} reaches 0, the attacker can move into the {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} for a decisive battle."

msgid "INTERFACE@TEXT@SIEGE@HYPERLINK"
msgstr "[hyperlink,GLOBAL.SiegeConcept]Siege[/hyperlink]"

