msgid "TOMEOFWONDERS@TERRAFORMING@DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Terraforming effects can change the appearance and <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceFeatureConcept.Hyperlink}>> in a {GLOBAL.ProvinceConcept.Hyperlink}. Terraforming can change what <<m:{GLOBAL.ProvinceImprovementConcept.Hyperlink}>> can be built in a Province, but does not destroy or change already built Province Improvements.[br/][br/]When terraforming originates from a source, such as a {GLOBAL.CityConcept.Hyperlink} or Province Improvement, then removing the source will revert the terraforming effects. When there is no source that can be removed, terraforming is permanent until overwritten by a new terraforming effect.[br/][br/]<<m:{GLOBAL.WorldMapSpellConcept.Hyperlink}>> can apply terraforming effects. When you cancel a sustained effect such as a {GLOBAL.SustainedWorldSpellConcept.Hyperlink}, its terraforming changes will not be reverted.[br/][br/]Certain provinces or features, such as Lava, Water, and Uninhabitable provinces, cannot normally be terraformed."

